// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 學測/IELTS/TOEFL Topic 17
window.I17_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Painting & Drawing 繪畫與素描","cards":[{"w":"painter","p":"n.","d":"a person who paints pictures","c":"畫家","s":"My aunt is a painter who works in a small studio by the river, and she sells her pictures at the weekend market.","t":"我阿姨是一位畫家,在河邊的小工作室工作,而且她週末會在市集賣她的畫。"},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"strong cloth that artists paint on","c":"畫布","s":"The art teacher gave each of us a large white canvas, but I felt nervous because I did not know what to paint.","t":"美術老師給我們每人一張大大的白色畫布,但我覺得很緊張,因為我不知道要畫什麼。"},{"w":"easel","p":"n.","d":"a wooden stand that holds a painting while you work","c":"畫架","s":"She set up her easel near the window to catch the morning light, and then she started to paint the old temple.","t":"她把畫架架在窗邊以捕捉早晨的光線,然後開始畫那座古老的廟宇。"},{"w":"palette","p":"n.","d":"a flat board for mixing paint colours","c":"調色盤","s":"He squeezed some blue and yellow onto his palette, and he mixed them slowly until he got the green colour of the hills.","t":"他在調色盤上擠了一些藍色和黃色,並慢慢調和,直到調出山丘的綠色。"},{"w":"paintbrush","p":"n.","d":"a brush used for putting paint on a surface","c":"畫筆","s":"Remember to wash your paintbrush in clean water after class, or the paint will dry and the hairs will become hard.","t":"下課後記得用清水洗你的畫筆,否則顏料會乾掉,刷毛會變硬。"},{"w":"watercolour","p":"n.","d":"paint mixed with water; a picture made this way","c":"水彩","s":"I prefer watercolour to oil paint because it dries quickly, but it is hard to fix a mistake once the colour is on paper.","t":"我比較喜歡水彩而不是油畫顏料,因為它乾得快,但顏色一上紙就很難修改錯誤。"},{"w":"oil paint","p":"n.phr.","d":"thick paint made with oil that dries slowly","c":"油畫顏料","s":"oil paint takes several days to dry completely, so the artist works on two or three pictures at the same time.","t":"油畫顏料需要好幾天才能完全乾燥,所以這位畫家會同時進行兩、三幅畫。"},{"w":"acrylic","p":"adj.","d":"made with a fast-drying plastic-based paint","c":"壓克力的","s":"We used acrylic paint for the school mural because it is cheap and bright, and it does not wash away in the rain.","t":"我們用壓克力顏料畫學校的壁畫,因為它便宜又鮮豔,而且不會被雨水沖掉。"},{"w":"brushstroke","p":"n.","d":"a single mark made by a paintbrush","c":"筆觸","s":"If you stand close to the painting, you can see every thick brushstroke, but from far away the picture looks smooth and calm.","t":"如果你站在畫作附近,可以看到每一道厚厚的筆觸,但從遠處看,畫面看起來平滑又寧靜。"},{"w":"still life","p":"n.phr.","d":"a picture of objects such as fruit, flowers or bottles","c":"靜物畫","s":"For homework we had to paint a still life of fruit on the kitchen table, so I arranged some apples next to a teapot.","t":"作業是要畫一幅廚房桌上水果的靜物畫,所以我把幾顆蘋果擺在茶壺旁邊。"},{"w":"portrait","p":"n.","d":"a painting, drawing or photo of a person","c":"肖像畫","s":"The family asked a local artist to paint a portrait of their grandfather, and they hung it in the living room for his ninetieth birthday.","t":"這家人請當地一位藝術家為爺爺畫一幅肖像畫,並在他九十歲生日時把它掛在客廳。"},{"w":"self-portrait","p":"n.","d":"a picture an artist makes of himself or herself","c":"自畫像","s":"Van Gogh painted more than thirty versions of his self-portrait, because he was poor and could not pay models to sit for him.","t":"梵谷畫了三十多幅自畫像,因為他很窮,付不起錢請模特兒讓他畫。"},{"w":"landscape painting","p":"n.phr.","d":"a picture of natural scenery such as hills or rivers","c":"風景畫","s":"Traditional Chinese landscape painting often shows tiny people under huge mountains, and this reminds viewers how small humans are in nature.","t":"傳統中國山水風景畫常描繪巨大山脈下渺小的人物,這提醒觀者人類在自然中是多麼渺小。"},{"w":"mural","p":"n.","d":"a large picture painted on a wall","c":"壁畫","s":"Students painted a colourful mural on the wall of the old train station, and now tourists stop there to take photos.","t":"學生們在舊火車站的牆上畫了一幅色彩繽紛的壁畫,現在遊客會在那裡停下來拍照。"},{"w":"vanishing point","p":"n.phr.","d":"the point where parallel lines seem to meet far away","c":"消失點","s":"Draw the road so that both sides meet at one vanishing point on the horizon, and the street will suddenly look very deep.","t":"把道路畫成兩側在地平線上的同一個消失點交會,街道就會突然看起來很有深度。"},{"w":"foreground","p":"n.","d":"the part of a picture that looks nearest to you","c":"前景","s":"In the foreground of the photo you can see a small dog, while the mountains stand quietly far behind it.","t":"在這張照片的前景中你可以看到一隻小狗,而山脈則靜靜地矗立在牠後方遠處。"},{"w":"background","p":"n.","d":"the part of a picture that looks farthest away","c":"背景","s":"The girl in the painting wears a red dress, but the background is dark grey, so she really stands out.","t":"畫中的女孩穿著紅色洋裝,但背景是深灰色的,所以她非常突出。"},{"w":"shading","p":"n.","d":"darker areas in a drawing that show shadow and shape","c":"陰影明暗","s":"Without any shading, your drawing of the ball looks flat, so add some dark pencil marks on one side.","t":"沒有任何陰影明暗,你畫的球看起來很扁平,所以在一側加上一些深色鉛筆線條吧。"},{"w":"hue","p":"n.","d":"a colour or shade of a colour","c":"色調;色相","s":"The sky turned a warm orange hue just before sunset, and the photographer quickly took out his camera.","t":"就在日落前,天空變成溫暖的橘色色調,攝影師趕緊拿出相機。"},{"w":"primary colour","p":"n.phr.","d":"red, yellow or blue, which mix to make other colours","c":"原色","s":"Red is a primary colour, and when you mix it with yellow you get orange, so you only need a few tubes of paint.","t":"紅色是一種原色,把它和黃色混合就會得到橘色,所以你只需要幾管顏料。"},{"w":"charcoal","p":"n.","d":"a black stick of burnt wood used for drawing","c":"炭筆","s":"He drew the old fisherman's face in charcoal, and his fingers became completely black by the end of the lesson.","t":"他用炭筆畫老漁夫的臉,到課程結束時他的手指全都變黑了。"},{"w":"pastel","p":"n.","d":"a soft coloured chalk stick used for drawing","c":"粉彩筆","s":"My little sister loves drawing with pastel because the colours are soft, but the dust gets all over her clothes.","t":"我妹妹喜歡用粉彩筆畫畫,因為顏色很柔和,但粉末會沾得她滿身都是。"},{"w":"sketchbook","p":"n.","d":"a book of blank pages for drawing","c":"素描本","s":"She always carries a small sketchbook in her bag, so she can draw interesting people on the MRT.","t":"她的包包裡總是帶著一本小素描本,這樣她就能在捷運上畫有趣的人。"},{"w":"doodle","p":"v.","d":"to draw small pictures without thinking carefully","c":"隨手塗鴉","s":"I often doodle in the margins of my notebook during long meetings, but it actually helps me listen better.","t":"我在冗長的會議中常在筆記本空白處隨手塗鴉,但這其實幫助我聽得更專心。"},{"w":"illustrator","p":"n.","d":"an artist who draws pictures for books or magazines","c":"插畫家","s":"The illustrator spent six months drawing pictures for the children's book, and the story became much more exciting.","t":"那位插畫家花了六個月為這本童書繪製插圖,故事因此變得精彩許多。"},{"w":"cartoonist","p":"n.","d":"a person who draws funny pictures or comic strips","c":"漫畫家","s":"The famous cartoonist draws a funny picture for the newspaper every day, and readers often laugh about politics because of him.","t":"這位知名的漫畫家每天為報紙畫一幅有趣的漫畫,讀者常因為他而對政治一笑置之。"},{"w":"frame","p":"n.","d":"the border of wood or metal around a picture","c":"畫框","s":"We bought a simple wooden frame for my daughter's drawing, and now it hangs proudly in the hallway.","t":"我們為女兒的畫買了一個簡單的木製畫框,現在它驕傲地掛在走廊上。"},{"w":"tone","p":"n.","d":"how light or dark a colour is","c":"色調明暗","s":"The artist used a soft blue tone for the whole picture, so the scene feels calm and a little sad.","t":"這位畫家整幅畫都用柔和的藍色色調,所以畫面感覺寧靜又帶點憂傷。"},{"w":"blend","p":"v.","d":"to mix colours smoothly together","c":"混合;暈染","s":"Use your finger to blend the two colours at the edge, and the sky will change gently from pink to purple.","t":"用手指在邊緣暈染這兩種顏色,天空就會從粉紅色柔和地漸變成紫色。"},{"w":"colour wheel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a circle that shows how colours relate to each other","c":"色相環","s":"Our teacher showed us a colour wheel, and we learned that colours opposite each other look very strong together.","t":"老師給我們看一個色相環,我們學到彼此相對的顏色放在一起看起來非常強烈。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Sculpture, Crafts & Materials 雕塑、工藝與媒材","cards":[{"w":"sculpture","p":"n.","d":"a work of art made by shaping stone, wood or metal","c":"雕塑","s":"A huge metal sculpture stands in front of the city hall, and children like to climb on its smooth base.","t":"一座巨大的金屬雕塑矗立在市政府前,孩子們喜歡爬上它光滑的底座。"},{"w":"sculptor","p":"n.","d":"an artist who makes sculptures","c":"雕塑家","s":"The sculptor worked on the stone lion for two years, but he refused to show anyone until it was finished.","t":"這位雕塑家花了兩年雕刻這隻石獅,但在完成前他拒絕讓任何人看。"},{"w":"sculpt","p":"v.","d":"to make a shape from stone, wood or clay","c":"雕塑;塑造","s":"During the summer camp, the kids learned to sculpt animals from soft soap, and they proudly took them home to their parents.","t":"夏令營期間,孩子們學會用柔軟的肥皂雕塑動物,並驕傲地把作品帶回家給父母。"},{"w":"chisel","p":"n.","d":"a metal tool with a sharp end for cutting wood or stone","c":"鑿子","s":"He hit the chisel gently with a hammer, and small pieces of wood fell to the floor around him.","t":"他用鐵鎚輕敲鑿子,小木屑掉落在他周圍的地板上。"},{"w":"wax","p":"n.","d":"a soft substance used to make candles and models","c":"蠟","s":"The museum shows famous people made of wax, so visitors take selfies with them although they are not real.","t":"這間博物館展示用蠟做成的名人像,所以雖然他們不是真人,遊客還是會和他們自拍。"},{"w":"cast","p":"v.","d":"to make an object by pouring hot metal into a shape","c":"鑄造","s":"The workers cast the bronze bell in a special mould, and then they waited a whole week for it to cool down.","t":"工人們在特製的模具中鑄造這口銅鐘,然後等了一整個星期讓它冷卻。"},{"w":"carve","p":"v.","d":"to cut wood or stone into a shape","c":"雕刻","s":"My grandfather likes to carve small birds from old pieces of wood, and he gives them to his grandchildren as gifts.","t":"我爺爺喜歡用舊木頭雕刻小鳥,並把它們當禮物送給孫子孫女。"},{"w":"installation","p":"n.","d":"a large artwork that fills a room or space","c":"裝置藝術","s":"The installation filled the whole room with hanging paper lanterns, so visitors felt as if they were walking through a dream.","t":"這件裝置藝術用懸掛的紙燈籠填滿整個房間,讓觀眾彷彿走在夢境之中。"},{"w":"potter","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes pots and dishes from clay","c":"陶藝家","s":"The potter in Yingge let us try making a cup, but mine looked strange because the clay kept moving.","t":"鶯歌的陶藝家讓我們試做一個杯子,但我的看起來很奇怪,因為陶土一直移動。"},{"w":"potter's wheel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a turning round plate used to shape clay","c":"拉坯轉盤","s":"She sat at the potter's wheel for hours, and she slowly shaped the wet clay into a tall, thin vase.","t":"她在拉坯轉盤前坐了好幾個小時,慢慢把濕陶土塑成一個又高又細的花瓶。"},{"w":"glaze","p":"n.","d":"a shiny coating put on pottery before it is fired","c":"釉","s":"After the bowls dried, we painted a blue glaze on them, so they became shiny and waterproof after firing.","t":"碗乾了之後,我們在上面塗了一層藍色的釉,所以燒製後它們變得光亮又防水。"},{"w":"embroidery","p":"n.","d":"pictures sewn onto cloth with coloured thread","c":"刺繡","s":"Her grandmother's embroidery shows flowers and birds in bright silk thread, and every tiny stitch was made by hand.","t":"她奶奶的刺繡用鮮豔的絲線描繪花鳥,每一個小針腳都是手工縫製的。"},{"w":"knit","p":"v.","d":"to make clothes from wool using two long needles","c":"編織;打毛線","s":"My mother likes to knit scarves in winter, and she usually gives them to friends before Chinese New Year.","t":"我媽媽冬天喜歡打毛線織圍巾,而且她通常會在農曆新年前把圍巾送給朋友。"},{"w":"quilt","p":"n.","d":"a warm bed cover made of many pieces of cloth","c":"拼布被","s":"The women in the village made a quilt from old clothes, and each square tells a story about a family.","t":"村裡的婦女用舊衣服做了一條拼布被,每一塊方格都訴說著一個家庭的故事。"},{"w":"origami","p":"n.","d":"the Japanese art of folding paper into shapes","c":"摺紙","s":"We learned origami in art class and folded a hundred paper cranes, because our classmate was sick in hospital.","t":"我們在美術課學了摺紙,折了一百隻紙鶴,因為我們的同學生病住院了。"},{"w":"paper-cutting","p":"n.","d":"the art of cutting paper into pretty patterns","c":"剪紙","s":"Red paper-cutting decorations appear on many windows during Lunar New Year, and they usually show lucky words or animals.","t":"農曆新年期間,許多窗戶上都會出現紅色的剪紙裝飾,通常是吉祥字或動物圖案。"},{"w":"woodcut","p":"n.","d":"a print made from a picture cut into wood","c":"木刻版畫","s":"The artist carved the design into a block of wood, and then she pressed it on paper to make a woodcut.","t":"這位藝術家把圖案刻在木塊上,然後壓印在紙上製作出一幅木刻版畫。"},{"w":"stained glass","p":"n.phr.","d":"coloured glass used to make pictures in windows","c":"彩繪玻璃","s":"Sunlight shone through the stained glass windows of the church, and colourful patterns danced across the floor.","t":"陽光穿過教堂的彩繪玻璃窗,繽紛的圖案在地板上舞動。"},{"w":"collage","p":"n.","d":"a picture made by sticking paper and photos onto a surface","c":"拼貼畫","s":"We cut pictures out of old magazines to make a collage about our dreams, and the teacher hung them on the classroom wall.","t":"我們從舊雜誌剪下圖片,做了一幅關於夢想的拼貼畫,老師把它們掛在教室牆上。"},{"w":"craft fair","p":"n.phr.","d":"an event where people sell things they have made by hand","c":"手作市集","s":"I bought a handmade leather wallet at the craft fair last weekend, and the seller even printed my name on it.","t":"上週末我在手作市集買了一個手工皮夾,賣家甚至幫我在上面印了名字。"},{"w":"handicraft","p":"n.","d":"a skilled activity of making things by hand","c":"手工藝","s":"Many tourists buy local handicraft such as bamboo baskets, because they want a real souvenir rather than a cheap plastic toy.","t":"許多遊客會買竹籃之類的在地手工藝品,因為他們想要真正的紀念品,而不是廉價的塑膠玩具。"},{"w":"jewellery","p":"n.","d":"rings, necklaces and other decorations you wear","c":"珠寶首飾","s":"She designs silver jewellery in her small workshop, and she sells her rings and necklaces online to customers around the world.","t":"她在小工作室裡設計銀首飾,並在網路上把戒指和項鍊賣給世界各地的顧客。"},{"w":"goldsmith","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes things from gold","c":"金匠","s":"The goldsmith melted the old gold chain carefully, and then he made it into a beautiful wedding ring for the young couple.","t":"這位金匠小心地熔化舊金鍊,然後為這對年輕夫妻把它打造成一枚美麗的婚戒。"},{"w":"lacquer","p":"n.","d":"a shiny liquid painted on wood to protect and decorate it","c":"漆","s":"The wooden box is covered with red lacquer, and it looks so shiny that you can almost see your face in it.","t":"這個木盒塗滿了紅漆,看起來亮到你幾乎能在上面看到自己的臉。"},{"w":"stencil","p":"n.","d":"a sheet with a shape cut out, used to paint the same shape","c":"鏤空模板","s":"The street artist held a stencil against the wall and sprayed paint over it, so the same bird appeared in seconds.","t":"這位街頭藝術家把鏤空模板貼在牆上並噴漆,同樣的鳥圖案幾秒內就出現了。"},{"w":"metalwork","p":"n.","d":"objects made from metal by skilled workers","c":"金工","s":"The exhibition shows beautiful metalwork from old temples, such as bronze lamps and iron gates with flowers on them.","t":"這個展覽展示了來自古廟的精美金工作品,例如青銅燈和帶有花朵圖案的鐵門。"},{"w":"bust","p":"n.","d":"a sculpture of a person's head and shoulders","c":"半身像","s":"A marble bust of the school's founder stands in the hall, and students sometimes put a hat on it for fun.","t":"學校創辦人的大理石半身像立在大廳裡,學生有時會為了好玩幫它戴上帽子。"},{"w":"workmanship","p":"n.","d":"the skill with which something is made","c":"做工;手藝","s":"The chair is over a hundred years old, but it is still strong because the workmanship is excellent.","t":"這張椅子已經超過一百歲了,但它依然堅固,因為做工非常精良。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Artists, Styles & Movements 藝術家、風格與流派","cards":[{"w":"Impressionism","p":"n.","d":"a style of painting that shows light and quick impressions","c":"印象派","s":"Impressionism began in France in the 1870s, and its painters often worked outdoors to catch changing light on water and fields.","t":"印象派於1870年代在法國興起,其畫家常在戶外作畫,以捕捉水面和田野上變幻的光線。"},{"w":"Impressionist","p":"n.","d":"a painter in the style of Impressionism","c":"印象派畫家","s":"Monet was a famous Impressionist, and he painted the same pond again and again because the light changed every hour.","t":"莫內是一位著名的印象派畫家,他一再畫同一座池塘,因為光線每小時都在變化。"},{"w":"Cubism","p":"n.","d":"an art style that shows objects as many geometric shapes","c":"立體派","s":"In Cubism, a face may be shown from the front and the side at the same time, so the picture can look confusing at first.","t":"在立體派中,一張臉可能同時從正面和側面呈現,所以畫面一開始可能看起來令人困惑。"},{"w":"Surrealism","p":"n.","d":"an art style that shows strange, dreamlike scenes","c":"超現實主義","s":"Surrealism was inspired by dreams, so its paintings often show melting clocks or fish flying through the sky.","t":"超現實主義受到夢境啟發,所以它的畫作常出現融化的時鐘或在天空飛翔的魚。"},{"w":"surreal","p":"adj.","d":"very strange, like a dream","c":"超現實的;離奇的","s":"Walking through the empty city at dawn felt surreal, because the streets that are usually so busy were completely silent.","t":"黎明時走過空蕩的城市感覺很離奇,因為平常熱鬧的街道完全寂靜無聲。"},{"w":"Expressionism","p":"n.","d":"an art style that shows strong feelings rather than real appearance","c":"表現主義","s":"Expressionism uses wild colours and twisted shapes, because the artists wanted to show fear and anger rather than real faces.","t":"表現主義使用狂野的色彩和扭曲的形狀,因為藝術家想表現恐懼和憤怒,而不是真實的面孔。"},{"w":"pop art","p":"n.phr.","d":"art that uses images from advertising and popular culture","c":"普普藝術","s":"pop art turned soup cans and comic books into famous paintings, and it made people ask what art really is.","t":"普普藝術把湯罐頭和漫畫書變成名畫,也讓人們思考藝術究竟是什麼。"},{"w":"realism","p":"n.","d":"showing things as they really are","c":"寫實主義","s":"The painter is known for his realism, and his pictures of tired farmers look almost like photographs.","t":"這位畫家以寫實主義聞名,他筆下疲憊的農民看起來幾乎就像照片一樣。"},{"w":"Romanticism","p":"n.","d":"an art movement that valued emotion, nature and imagination","c":"浪漫主義","s":"Romanticism painters loved stormy seas and dark forests, because they believed nature could make people feel strong emotions.","t":"浪漫主義畫家熱愛暴風雨的海洋和幽暗的森林,因為他們相信大自然能讓人產生強烈的情感。"},{"w":"Baroque","p":"adj.","d":"in a rich, dramatic European style of the 1600s","c":"巴洛克風格的","s":"The Baroque church is full of gold decorations and dramatic paintings, so visitors usually look up at the ceiling in silence.","t":"這座巴洛克風格的教堂到處是金色裝飾和戲劇性的畫作,所以遊客通常會靜靜地抬頭仰望天花板。"},{"w":"Gothic","p":"adj.","d":"in a medieval style with tall pointed arches","c":"哥德式的","s":"The Gothic cathedral has tall pointed windows, and it took almost two hundred years for the builders to finish it.","t":"這座哥德式的大教堂有高聳的尖窗,而工匠們花了將近兩百年才完成它。"},{"w":"avant-garde","p":"adj.","d":"very new and experimental in art or ideas","c":"前衛的","s":"The theatre group performs avant-garde plays without any words, so some audiences love them while others leave early.","t":"這個劇團演出沒有任何台詞的前衛戲劇,所以有些觀眾很喜愛,而有些則提早離場。"},{"w":"contemporary art","p":"n.phr.","d":"art made in recent times","c":"當代藝術","s":"Many people find contemporary art hard to understand, but the guide explained each work, so our visit became much more interesting.","t":"許多人覺得當代藝術難以理解,但導覽員解說了每件作品,所以我們的參觀變得有趣多了。"},{"w":"conceptual art","p":"n.phr.","d":"art in which the idea matters more than the object","c":"觀念藝術","s":"In conceptual art, the idea behind the work is more important than its skill, so a simple chair can become a serious artwork.","t":"在觀念藝術中,作品背後的想法比技巧更重要,所以一張簡單的椅子也能成為嚴肅的藝術品。"},{"w":"modern art","p":"n.phr.","d":"art from about the 1860s to the 1970s that broke old rules","c":"現代藝術","s":"My grandfather says that modern art looks like a child's drawing, but my sister explains why the artists broke the old rules.","t":"我爺爺說現代藝術看起來像小孩的塗鴉,但我姊姊解釋了為什麼藝術家要打破舊規則。"},{"w":"folk art","p":"n.phr.","d":"traditional art made by ordinary people in a region","c":"民俗藝術","s":"Hakka folk art includes painted umbrellas and simple cloth patterns, and it shows the daily life of country people.","t":"客家民俗藝術包括彩繪紙傘和簡樸的布料圖案,展現了鄉村百姓的日常生活。"},{"w":"art movement","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of artists who share ideas and a style for a period","c":"藝術運動;流派","s":"The young painters started a new art movement in Paris, because they were tired of the strict rules of the art academy.","t":"這群年輕畫家在巴黎發起一場新的藝術運動,因為他們厭倦了藝術學院的嚴格規範。"},{"w":"genre","p":"n.","d":"a type of art, music or writing","c":"類型","s":"Hip-hop is my favourite music genre, but my parents prefer old Taiwanese folk songs from their childhood.","t":"嘻哈是我最喜歡的音樂類型,但我爸媽比較喜歡他們童年時的台灣老民謠。"},{"w":"style","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of making art","c":"風格","s":"Each artist develops a personal style over many years, so experts can often recognise a painting before reading the name.","t":"每位藝術家都要花很多年發展個人風格,所以專家常常在看到名字之前就能認出畫作。"},{"w":"stylistic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the style of a work of art","c":"風格上的","s":"There are clear stylistic differences between his early and late paintings, because he lost much of his eyesight in old age.","t":"他早期和晚期的畫作有明顯的風格上的差異,因為他晚年視力大幅衰退。"},{"w":"masterpiece","p":"n.","d":"an extremely good work of art","c":"傑作","s":"Many people think the \"Mona Lisa\" is a masterpiece, but some visitors are surprised because the painting is quite small.","t":"許多人認為《蒙娜麗莎》是一件傑作,但有些參觀者很驚訝,因為這幅畫相當小。"},{"w":"old master","p":"n.phr.","d":"a great European painter from before about 1800","c":"古典大師","s":"The museum owns a painting by an old master from the 1600s, so it is kept behind thick glass and guarded day and night.","t":"博物館擁有一幅1600年代古典大師的畫作,所以它被放在厚玻璃後面,日夜都有人看守。"},{"w":"virtuoso","p":"n.","d":"a person with great skill, especially in music","c":"大師;名家","s":"The young pianist is a real virtuoso, and she can play the most difficult pieces without looking at the music.","t":"這位年輕鋼琴家是真正的名家,她不看樂譜就能彈奏最困難的曲子。"},{"w":"muse","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives an artist ideas and inspiration","c":"繆思;靈感來源","s":"The singer says his wife is his muse, because most of his love songs were written about her.","t":"這位歌手說他的妻子是他的繆思,因為他大部分的情歌都是為她寫的。"},{"w":"signature","p":"n.","d":"an artist's name written on a work","c":"簽名","s":"Experts checked the signature in the corner of the painting carefully, because they suspected that the picture was a copy.","t":"專家仔細檢查畫作角落的簽名,因為他們懷疑這幅畫是複製品。"},{"w":"bohemian","p":"adj.","d":"living in an unusual, free way like many artists","c":"波希米亞風的;放蕩不羈的","s":"They live a bohemian life in a small flat full of paintings, and they rarely care about money or fashion.","t":"他們在堆滿畫作的小公寓裡過著放蕩不羈的生活,而且很少在乎金錢或時尚。"},{"w":"eccentric","p":"adj.","d":"strange or unusual in behaviour","c":"古怪的","s":"The eccentric artist wore a bright purple suit every day, and he talked to his paintings as if they were friends.","t":"這位古怪的藝術家每天都穿亮紫色西裝,而且會跟他的畫作說話,彷彿它們是朋友。"},{"w":"posthumous","p":"adj.","d":"happening after a person's death","c":"死後的","s":"The poet enjoyed posthumous fame, because her poems became popular only after she died in poverty.","t":"這位詩人享有死後的名聲,因為她的詩直到她在貧困中過世後才受歡迎。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Galleries, Museums & the Art Market 美術館、博物館與藝術市場","cards":[{"w":"gallery","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where art is shown or sold","c":"畫廊;美術館","s":"We visited a small gallery in Taipei that shows young local artists, and the owner told us about each painting.","t":"我們參觀了台北一家展出在地年輕藝術家作品的小畫廊,老闆向我們介紹了每一幅畫。"},{"w":"museum","p":"n.","d":"a building where valuable objects are kept and shown","c":"博物館","s":"The National Palace museum is very crowded in summer, so we went early in the morning to avoid the tour groups.","t":"國立故宮博物院夏天非常擁擠,所以我們一大早就去,以避開旅行團。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of objects gathered together","c":"收藏","s":"The museum's collection includes more than five thousand paintings, but only a small number can be shown at one time.","t":"這間博物館的收藏包括五千多幅畫作,但一次只能展出其中一小部分。"},{"w":"collector","p":"n.","d":"a person who gathers valuable objects as a hobby","c":"收藏家","s":"The wealthy collector bought paintings for fifty years, and before he died he gave all of them to the city.","t":"這位富有的收藏家買了五十年的畫,並在過世前把它們全部捐給了這座城市。"},{"w":"auction","p":"n.","d":"a public sale where things go to the person who pays most","c":"拍賣會","s":"The painting was sold at auction for ten million dollars, and the crowd clapped loudly when the hammer came down.","t":"這幅畫在拍賣會上以一千萬美元售出,落槌時群眾大聲鼓掌。"},{"w":"auctioneer","p":"n.","d":"the person who runs an auction","c":"拍賣官","s":"The auctioneer spoke very fast and pointed at people who raised their hands, so I was afraid to scratch my head.","t":"拍賣官說話非常快,並指著舉手的人,所以我連抓頭都不敢。"},{"w":"bid","p":"v.","d":"to offer a price for something at an auction","c":"出價;競標","s":"Two collectors bid against each other for the old vase, and the price rose higher and higher every few seconds.","t":"兩位收藏家為這只古花瓶互相競標,價格每隔幾秒就越抬越高。"},{"w":"bidder","p":"n.","d":"a person who offers money at an auction","c":"競標者","s":"The painting went to an unknown bidder on the telephone, so nobody in the room knew who the new owner was.","t":"這幅畫由一位透過電話出價的匿名競標者得標,所以現場沒有人知道新主人是誰。"},{"w":"art dealer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who buys and sells works of art","c":"藝術經紀商;畫商","s":"An art dealer noticed her paintings online, and he offered to sell them in his gallery in Hong Kong.","t":"一位畫商在網路上注意到她的畫作,並提議在他香港的畫廊販售。"},{"w":"valuation","p":"n.","d":"a judgement of how much something is worth","c":"估價","s":"We took grandma's old painting for a valuation, but the expert said it was worth only a few hundred dollars.","t":"我們把奶奶的舊畫拿去估價,但專家說它只值幾百元。"},{"w":"priceless","p":"adj.","d":"so valuable that no price can be put on it","c":"無價的","s":"The museum's ancient scrolls are priceless, so they are kept in dark rooms where the temperature never changes.","t":"博物館的古代卷軸是無價的,所以它們被保存在溫度從不變化的暗室裡。"},{"w":"authenticate","p":"v.","d":"to prove that something is real and not a copy","c":"鑑定真偽","s":"Experts used X-rays to authenticate the painting, and they found an older picture hidden under the paint.","t":"專家使用X光來鑑定這幅畫的真偽,結果發現顏料底下藏著一幅更早的畫。"},{"w":"conservator","p":"n.","d":"a person who repairs and protects old works of art","c":"文物修復師","s":"The conservator spent months cleaning the dirty painting with tiny brushes, and the bright colours slowly appeared again.","t":"這位文物修復師花了好幾個月用小刷子清理骯髒的畫作,鮮豔的色彩慢慢重新顯現。"},{"w":"guided tour","p":"n.phr.","d":"a visit led by a person who explains things","c":"導覽","s":"We joined a free guided tour of the museum, and the guide told us funny stories about the artists' lives.","t":"我們參加了博物館的免費導覽,導覽員告訴我們藝術家生活中的趣事。"},{"w":"docent","p":"n.","d":"a trained guide who explains art in a museum","c":"導覽員","s":"The docent at the art museum is a retired teacher, and she explains the paintings so clearly that even children listen carefully.","t":"美術館的導覽員是一位退休老師,她解說畫作清楚到連孩子都認真聆聽。"},{"w":"audio guide","p":"n.phr.","d":"a recorded talk you listen to as you walk round a museum","c":"語音導覽","s":"I rented an audio guide at the entrance, so I could listen to information about each painting in Chinese.","t":"我在入口租了一台語音導覽,這樣就能聽到每幅畫的中文介紹。"},{"w":"gift shop","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop in a museum that sells souvenirs","c":"紀念品店","s":"After the exhibition we went to the gift shop, and I bought postcards of my favourite paintings for my friends.","t":"看完展覽後我們去了紀念品店,我買了我最喜歡的畫作明信片送給朋友。"},{"w":"opening night","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first evening of an exhibition or show","c":"開幕夜;首演之夜","s":"Hundreds of guests came to the opening night of her first exhibition, but she was so nervous that she hid in the bathroom.","t":"數百位賓客出席她首次個展的開幕夜,但她緊張到躲進了廁所。"},{"w":"art fair","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large event where galleries show and sell art","c":"藝術博覽會","s":"Galleries from twenty countries come to the art fair in Taipei every year, and collectors fly in to buy new works.","t":"每年有來自二十個國家的畫廊參加台北的藝術博覽會,收藏家也會搭機前來購買新作品。"},{"w":"biennale","p":"n.","d":"a large art exhibition held every two years","c":"雙年展","s":"The famous biennale in Venice takes place every two years, and artists from all over the world hope to be invited.","t":"威尼斯著名的雙年展每兩年舉辦一次,世界各地的藝術家都希望受邀參展。"},{"w":"art critic","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who writes opinions about art","c":"藝評家","s":"One well-known art critic called the exhibition boring, but thousands of young visitors still queued to see it.","t":"一位知名藝評家說這個展覽很無聊,但仍有數千名年輕觀眾排隊參觀。"},{"w":"loan","p":"n.","d":"something borrowed for a period of time","c":"出借;借展","s":"The famous painting is on loan from a museum in Paris, so it will return to France after three months.","t":"這幅名畫是巴黎一家博物館借展的,所以三個月後會回到法國。"},{"w":"heist","p":"n.","d":"a carefully planned robbery","c":"搶劫;竊案","s":"Thieves stole thirteen paintings in a famous art heist in 1990, and the frames still hang empty on the museum wall.","t":"竊賊在1990年一起著名的藝術品竊案中偷走了十三幅畫,那些空畫框至今仍掛在博物館牆上。"},{"w":"vandalise","p":"v.","d":"to damage property on purpose","c":"蓄意破壞","s":"Someone tried to vandalise the statue in the park last night, so the city has decided to put up cameras.","t":"昨晚有人試圖蓄意破壞公園裡的雕像,所以市政府決定裝設監視器。"},{"w":"pedestal","p":"n.","d":"a base on which a statue stands","c":"底座;基座","s":"The small bronze horse stands on a tall stone pedestal, so visitors can look at it at eye level.","t":"這匹小銅馬立在高高的石頭底座上,所以參觀者能平視欣賞它。"},{"w":"spotlight","p":"n.","d":"a strong light pointed at one thing","c":"聚光燈","s":"A single spotlight shone on the painting in the dark room, and it made the gold colours glow beautifully.","t":"一盞聚光燈照在暗室中的畫作上,讓金色光彩美麗地閃耀。"},{"w":"art market","p":"n.phr.","d":"the buying and selling of art","c":"藝術市場","s":"The art market in Asia has grown quickly, because more young people now see paintings as a good investment.","t":"亞洲的藝術市場成長迅速,因為現在更多年輕人把畫作視為好的投資。"},{"w":"price tag","p":"n.phr.","d":"the cost of something","c":"價格;標價","s":"The sculpture has a price tag of two million dollars, but the gallery says several buyers are already interested.","t":"這件雕塑的標價是兩百萬美元,但畫廊表示已經有好幾位買家感興趣。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Creativity & the Creative Process 創造力與創作過程","cards":[{"w":"creativity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make new and original things","c":"創造力","s":"The new art programme aims to develop students' creativity, so there are no right or wrong answers in class.","t":"新的藝術課程旨在培養學生的創造力,所以課堂上沒有標準答案。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new ideas or making things","c":"有創意的","s":"My cousin is very creative, and she turned old jeans into a bag that everyone at school wanted to buy.","t":"我表妹非常有創意,她把舊牛仔褲改成一個全校都想買的包包。"},{"w":"creator","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes something new","c":"創作者","s":"The creator of the popular cartoon was only twenty years old, but his drawings soon appeared on T-shirts everywhere.","t":"這部熱門卡通的創作者只有二十歲,但他的畫很快就出現在各地的T恤上。"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to form pictures and ideas in your mind","c":"想像力","s":"Children have a wonderful imagination, and a simple cardboard box can become a spaceship or a castle in their games.","t":"孩子們擁有奇妙的想像力,一個簡單的紙箱在他們的遊戲中就能變成太空船或城堡。"},{"w":"imagine","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture of something in your mind","c":"想像","s":"Close your eyes and imagine a quiet beach at sunset, and then try to paint the colours you see.","t":"閉上眼睛想像日落時寧靜的海灘,然後試著畫出你看到的顏色。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the wish or idea to do something","c":"啟發;激勵","s":"Her trip to Morocco helped inspire a new series of paintings, because the markets were full of bright colours.","t":"她的摩洛哥之旅啟發了一系列新畫作,因為那裡的市集充滿鮮豔的色彩。"},{"w":"inspired","p":"adj.","d":"having excellent, original qualities","c":"靈感十足的;絕妙的","s":"The director's inspired choice of music made the sad scene unforgettable, and many people in the cinema began to cry.","t":"導演絕妙的配樂選擇讓這悲傷的一幕令人難忘,電影院裡許多人都哭了。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"new and different from anything before","c":"原創的;獨創的","s":"The judges wanted original designs, so they rejected any poster that looked like something on the internet.","t":"評審想要原創的設計,所以他們淘汰了任何看起來像網路上作品的海報。"},{"w":"daydream","p":"v.","d":"to think pleasant thoughts that take you away from the present","c":"做白日夢","s":"I often daydream on the bus about future trips, but sometimes I miss my stop because I am not paying attention.","t":"我常在公車上做白日夢想著未來的旅行,但有時因為不專心而坐過站。"},{"w":"improvise","p":"v.","d":"to make or perform something without preparation","c":"即興創作;臨場發揮","s":"The actor forgot his lines, so he had to improvise, and the audience laughed because they thought it was part of the play.","t":"這位演員忘了台詞,所以他只好臨場發揮,觀眾都笑了,因為他們以為那是劇情的一部分。"},{"w":"improvisation","p":"n.","d":"performing without planning beforehand","c":"即興表演","s":"Jazz musicians are famous for improvisation, because they often create new tunes on stage without any written music.","t":"爵士樂手以即興表演聞名,因為他們常在台上不看樂譜就創作新曲調。"},{"w":"spontaneity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of acting naturally without planning","c":"自發性;隨性","s":"Children's drawings are full of spontaneity, while adults often worry too much about making mistakes.","t":"孩子的畫充滿隨性,而大人往往太擔心犯錯。"},{"w":"flair","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability to do something well","c":"天分;才華","s":"She has a real flair for design, and even her simple school projects look like professional magazine pages.","t":"她在設計方面很有天分,就連她簡單的學校作業看起來都像專業雜誌的版面。"},{"w":"talent","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability to do something well","c":"天賦","s":"He showed a great talent for drawing when he was five, so his parents sent him to art classes every Saturday.","t":"他五歲時就展現出很高的繪畫天賦,所以父母每週六都送他去上美術課。"},{"w":"artistic","p":"adj.","d":"showing skill in art","c":"有藝術天分的;藝術的","s":"My brother is very artistic, but he chose to study engineering because he worried about finding a job.","t":"我哥哥很有藝術天分,但他選擇念工程,因為他擔心找不到工作。"},{"w":"self-expression","p":"n.","d":"showing your feelings and ideas through art or actions","c":"自我表達","s":"Dance is a form of self-expression for many teenagers, because they can show feelings that are hard to put into words.","t":"對許多青少年來說,舞蹈是一種自我表達的方式,因為他們能展現難以言喻的感受。"},{"w":"divergent thinking","p":"n.phr.","d":"thinking of many different answers to one problem","c":"擴散性思考","s":"The teacher asked us to list fifty uses for a paper clip, because this exercise trains divergent thinking.","t":"老師要我們列出迴紋針的五十種用途,因為這個練習能訓練擴散性思考。"},{"w":"lateral thinking","p":"n.phr.","d":"solving problems in unusual and creative ways","c":"水平思考","s":"The puzzle seemed impossible, but lateral thinking helped us find a surprising answer that nobody expected.","t":"這道謎題似乎無解,但水平思考幫助我們找到一個出乎所有人意料的答案。"},{"w":"eureka moment","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sudden moment when you find a great idea","c":"靈光乍現的時刻","s":"The designer had a eureka moment in the shower, and she quickly wrote her idea on the steamy mirror.","t":"這位設計師在洗澡時靈光乍現,她趕緊把想法寫在起霧的鏡子上。"},{"w":"creative block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when you cannot produce new ideas","c":"創作瓶頸","s":"The songwriter suffered from a creative block for months, so he travelled to the mountains to find fresh ideas.","t":"這位詞曲創作者陷入創作瓶頸好幾個月,所以他到山上旅行尋找新靈感。"},{"w":"writer's block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when a writer cannot think what to write","c":"寫作瓶頸","s":"I had writer's block when I started my essay, but going for a short walk helped me think again.","t":"我開始寫論文時遇到寫作瓶頸,但出去散步一下幫助我重新思考。"},{"w":"playful","p":"adj.","d":"full of fun and not serious","c":"好玩的;俏皮的","s":"The artist uses playful shapes and bright colours, so even serious adults smile when they walk into her exhibition.","t":"這位藝術家運用俏皮的形狀和鮮豔的色彩,所以就連嚴肅的大人走進她的展覽也會微笑。"},{"w":"flow","p":"n.","d":"a happy state of complete focus on an activity","c":"心流","s":"When I paint, I sometimes enter a state of flow, and three hours pass without me noticing the time.","t":"我畫畫時有時會進入心流狀態,三個小時過去了我卻沒注意到時間。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"Good designers are always curious about how things work, so they ask many questions before they start drawing.","t":"好的設計師總是對事物如何運作感到好奇,所以他們在開始畫之前會問很多問題。"},{"w":"open-minded","p":"adj.","d":"willing to accept new and different ideas","c":"心胸開闊的","s":"Try to be open-minded when you visit a modern art museum, because some works look strange but have interesting meanings.","t":"參觀現代美術館時試著保持心胸開闊,因為有些作品看起來很怪,卻有有趣的含義。"},{"w":"risk-taking","p":"n.","d":"doing things that might fail in order to achieve something","c":"冒險","s":"Creative work often needs a little risk-taking, because many new ideas fail several times before they finally succeed.","t":"創作工作常常需要一點冒險,因為許多新點子在最終成功前會失敗好幾次。"},{"w":"mood board","p":"n.phr.","d":"a collection of pictures and colours used to plan a design","c":"情緒板;靈感板","s":"Before designing the café, she made a mood board with photos of plants and wood, so the owner could see her ideas.","t":"在設計咖啡廳之前,她做了一塊貼滿植物與木頭照片的靈感板,讓老闆能看到她的構想。"},{"w":"creative process","p":"n.phr.","d":"the steps people follow to make something new","c":"創作過程","s":"Every artist has a different creative process, and some begin with careful plans while others simply start painting.","t":"每位藝術家都有不同的創作過程,有些人從周密的計畫開始,而有些人則直接動筆。"},{"w":"craft","p":"v.","d":"to make something skilfully","c":"精心製作","s":"She spent weeks trying to craft the perfect opening line for her novel, but she rewrote it many times.","t":"她花了好幾週試圖精心寫出小說完美的開場白,但她改寫了很多次。"},{"w":"rework","p":"v.","d":"to change something in order to improve it","c":"修改;重做","s":"The editor asked the author to rework the ending, because readers found it too sad and confusing.","t":"編輯請作者修改結局,因為讀者覺得它太悲傷又令人困惑。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Photography, Design & Digital Art 攝影、設計與數位藝術","cards":[{"w":"photographer","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes photographs, often as a job","c":"攝影師","s":"The wedding photographer asked everyone to stand closer together, and then he climbed on a chair to take a group photo.","t":"婚禮攝影師請大家站近一點,然後他爬上椅子拍了一張團體照。"},{"w":"photography","p":"n.","d":"the art or job of taking photos","c":"攝影","s":"He became interested in photography when his grandfather gave him an old film camera on his sixteenth birthday.","t":"他在爺爺於他十六歲生日送他一台舊底片相機後,開始對攝影產生興趣。"},{"w":"snapshot","p":"n.","d":"a quick, informal photo","c":"快照;隨手拍","s":"I took a quick snapshot of my friends at the night market, and it became my favourite photo of the whole trip.","t":"我在夜市幫朋友隨手拍了一張照片,它成了整趟旅行中我最喜歡的照片。"},{"w":"tripod","p":"n.","d":"a three-legged stand that holds a camera steady","c":"三腳架","s":"You need a tripod to photograph stars at night, because even a tiny movement of your hands will make the picture blurry.","t":"晚上拍星星需要三腳架,因為即使手稍微晃動都會讓照片模糊。"},{"w":"shutter","p":"n.","d":"the part of a camera that opens to let in light","c":"快門","s":"Press the shutter button gently when the bird opens its wings, or you might miss the perfect moment.","t":"在鳥張開翅膀時輕按快門鍵,否則你可能會錯過完美的瞬間。"},{"w":"aperture","p":"n.","d":"the hole in a camera lens that controls light","c":"光圈","s":"A wide aperture lets in more light, so it is useful when you take photos in a dark restaurant.","t":"大光圈能讓更多光線進入,所以在昏暗的餐廳拍照時很有用。"},{"w":"zoom","p":"v.","d":"to make something look closer with a camera","c":"拉近;放大","s":"The photographer had to zoom in on the shy deer, because it would run away if he walked any closer.","t":"攝影師必須把鏡頭拉近拍那隻害羞的鹿,因為他再走近一點牠就會跑掉。"},{"w":"close-up","p":"n.","d":"a photo taken from very near","c":"特寫","s":"The film begins with a close-up of the girl's eyes, so the audience immediately feels her fear.","t":"這部電影以女孩雙眼的特寫開場,所以觀眾立刻感受到她的恐懼。"},{"w":"flash","p":"n.","d":"a bright light on a camera for dark places","c":"閃光燈","s":"Please turn off your flash inside the museum, because strong light can slowly damage old paintings.","t":"在博物館裡請關閉閃光燈,因為強光會慢慢損害古老的畫作。"},{"w":"darkroom","p":"n.","d":"a dark room for developing film photos","c":"暗房","s":"In the school darkroom, we watched the picture slowly appear on the paper, and it felt like magic.","t":"在學校的暗房裡,我們看著影像慢慢浮現在相紙上,感覺就像魔法一樣。"},{"w":"black-and-white","p":"adj.","d":"showing only black, white and grey","c":"黑白的","s":"She prefers black-and-white photos of old streets, because she thinks colour makes them look too modern.","t":"她比較喜歡老街的黑白照片,因為她認為彩色會讓它們看起來太現代。"},{"w":"graphic design","p":"n.phr.","d":"the art of combining words and pictures for posters, websites etc.","c":"平面設計","s":"My sister studies graphic design at university, and she designed the logo for our family's noodle shop.","t":"我姊姊在大學念平面設計,她為我們家的麵店設計了招牌標誌。"},{"w":"graphic designer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who designs posters, books or websites","c":"平面設計師","s":"The company hired a graphic designer to make its website look modern, and sales rose within a few months.","t":"這家公司聘請了一位平面設計師讓網站看起來更現代,幾個月內業績就上升了。"},{"w":"typography","p":"n.","d":"the style and arrangement of printed letters","c":"字體排印","s":"Good typography makes a menu easy to read, but a strange font can make customers feel confused.","t":"好的字體排印讓菜單容易閱讀,但奇怪的字型會讓顧客感到困惑。"},{"w":"font","p":"n.","d":"a set of letters in one style and size","c":"字型","s":"Please use a simple font for your report, because the fancy one is hard for the teacher to read.","t":"你的報告請用簡單的字型,因為花俏的字型老師很難閱讀。"},{"w":"colour scheme","p":"n.phr.","d":"the set of colours chosen for a design","c":"配色","s":"We chose a calm colour scheme of light blue and white for the bedroom, so it feels peaceful at night.","t":"我們為臥室選了淺藍和白色的沉穩配色,所以晚上感覺很寧靜。"},{"w":"digital art","p":"n.phr.","d":"art made with computers or tablets","c":"數位藝術","s":"digital art has become very popular with teenagers, because they can draw on a tablet and share the work online at once.","t":"數位藝術在青少年間變得非常受歡迎,因為他們能在平板上作畫並立刻上網分享。"},{"w":"pixel","p":"n.","d":"one of the tiny dots that make a digital image","c":"像素","s":"If you make the photo too large, you will see every pixel, so the picture will look blocky.","t":"如果你把照片放得太大,就會看到每一個像素,所以畫面會看起來像方塊。"},{"w":"animation","p":"n.","d":"moving pictures made from drawings or computer images","c":"動畫","s":"Japanese animation is loved around the world, and some films take years to finish because every scene is drawn by hand.","t":"日本動畫受到全世界喜愛,有些電影要花數年才能完成,因為每一幕都是手繪的。"},{"w":"animator","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes animated films","c":"動畫師","s":"The animator drew twelve pictures for every second of the film, so a short scene took him several weeks.","t":"這位動畫師為影片的每一秒畫了十二張圖,所以一個短短的場景就花了他好幾週。"},{"w":"NFT","p":"n.","d":"a digital certificate that shows who owns a digital artwork","c":"非同質化代幣","s":"He sold a cartoon cat as an NFT for a lot of money, but a year later nobody wanted to buy it.","t":"他把一隻卡通貓以非同質化代幣的形式賣了很多錢,但一年後就沒人想買了。"},{"w":"AI-generated","p":"adj.","d":"made by artificial intelligence, not a person","c":"人工智慧生成的","s":"The AI-generated picture won first prize in the contest, so many human artists complained that the result was unfair.","t":"那幅人工智慧生成的圖片在比賽中贏得首獎,所以許多人類藝術家抱怨結果不公平。"},{"w":"retouch","p":"v.","d":"to improve a photo by making small changes","c":"修圖","s":"Magazines often retouch photos of models to hide spots, but this gives young readers unrealistic ideas about beauty.","t":"雜誌常修圖遮掉模特兒臉上的斑點,但這讓年輕讀者對美產生不切實際的想法。"},{"w":"photo shoot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a session when a photographer takes many photos","c":"拍攝工作","s":"The band had a photo shoot on the beach for their new album, but the strong wind kept blowing the singer's hair.","t":"樂團為新專輯在海灘進行拍攝工作,但強風一直吹亂主唱的頭髮。"},{"w":"stylus","p":"n.","d":"a pen-shaped tool for drawing on a screen","c":"觸控筆","s":"She draws her comics with a stylus on a tablet, so she can easily fix mistakes with one click.","t":"她用觸控筆在平板上畫漫畫,所以只要點一下就能輕鬆修正錯誤。"},{"w":"visual effects","p":"n.phr.","d":"images added to films by computer","c":"視覺特效","s":"The film used amazing visual effects to show dragons flying over the city, and it won an award for them.","t":"這部電影運用驚人的視覺特效呈現飛越城市的巨龍,並因此獲獎。"},{"w":"cartoon","p":"n.","d":"a funny drawing or animated film","c":"卡通;漫畫","s":"My little brother watches a cartoon every morning before school, and he copies the characters' funny voices all day.","t":"我弟弟每天早上上學前都會看一部卡通,然後一整天模仿角色的搞笑聲音。"},{"w":"comic book","p":"n.phr.","d":"a magazine that tells stories in pictures","c":"漫畫書","s":"I learned many English words from reading a comic book every week, because the pictures helped me guess the meanings.","t":"我每週讀一本漫畫書,從中學到很多英文單字,因為圖片幫助我猜出意思。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Performing Arts & Music 表演藝術與音樂","cards":[{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of entertaining an audience","c":"表演;演出","s":"Her performance in the school play was so moving that several parents wiped tears from their eyes.","t":"她在學校話劇中的演出非常感人,好幾位家長都擦了眼淚。"},{"w":"performer","p":"n.","d":"a person who entertains an audience","c":"表演者","s":"Each performer at the festival had only ten minutes on stage, so they practised their acts many times.","t":"節慶上每位表演者只有十分鐘的上台時間,所以他們把表演練習了很多次。"},{"w":"theatre","p":"n.","d":"a building where plays are performed","c":"劇院","s":"We went to the theatre to see a musical on Saturday, but the tickets were so expensive that we sat in the back row.","t":"週六我們去劇院看音樂劇,但票價太貴了,所以我們坐在最後一排。"},{"w":"playwright","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes plays","c":"劇作家","s":"The young playwright wrote a play about her grandmother's life, and it sold out every night for a month.","t":"這位年輕劇作家寫了一齣關於她奶奶一生的戲,連續一個月每晚都售罄。"},{"w":"rehearse","p":"v.","d":"to practise a play or music before a performance","c":"排練","s":"The choir had to rehearse every evening for a month, because the concert was only a few weeks away.","t":"合唱團一個月來每晚都得排練,因為音樂會只剩幾週了。"},{"w":"backstage","p":"adv.","d":"behind the stage in a theatre","c":"在後台","s":"The dancers waited nervously backstage before the show, while the audience slowly found their seats.","t":"演出前舞者們緊張地在後台等待,而觀眾則慢慢找到座位。"},{"w":"audition","p":"n.","d":"a short performance to get a role in a show","c":"試鏡;甄選","s":"She practised the song for weeks before the audition, and she was thrilled when she got the main role.","t":"她在試鏡前把那首歌練了好幾週,當她拿到主角時非常興奮。"},{"w":"choreographer","p":"n.","d":"a person who plans the movements of a dance","c":"編舞家","s":"The choreographer changed the dance three times in one week, so the dancers felt exhausted and confused.","t":"編舞家一週內改了三次舞步,所以舞者們感到筋疲力盡又困惑。"},{"w":"choreography","p":"n.","d":"the planned steps and movements of a dance","c":"編舞;舞步設計","s":"The choreography of the K-pop song is very difficult, but thousands of fans have learned it from online videos.","t":"這首韓流歌曲的舞步設計非常困難,但數千名粉絲已經透過網路影片學會了。"},{"w":"ballet","p":"n.","d":"a graceful type of dance that tells a story","c":"芭蕾舞","s":"My niece has taken ballet lessons since she was four, and she dreams of dancing in \"Swan Lake\" one day.","t":"我姪女從四歲就開始上芭蕾舞課,她夢想有一天能在《天鵝湖》中跳舞。"},{"w":"orchestra","p":"n.","d":"a large group of musicians who play together","c":"管弦樂團","s":"The school orchestra has sixty students, and they play a free concert in the park every spring.","t":"學校的管弦樂團有六十名學生,他們每年春天都會在公園舉辦免費音樂會。"},{"w":"composer","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes music","c":"作曲家","s":"The film's composer wrote the music in only three weeks, but it became one of the most famous soundtracks in the world.","t":"這部電影的作曲家只花三週就寫完配樂,但它成為世上最著名的電影原聲帶之一。"},{"w":"compose","p":"v.","d":"to write music","c":"作曲","s":"Mozart began to compose music when he was five, and he wrote more than six hundred pieces in his short life.","t":"莫札特五歲就開始作曲,他在短暫的一生中寫了六百多首作品。"},{"w":"melody","p":"n.","d":"a tune; a series of musical notes","c":"旋律","s":"The melody of the song is very simple, so even small children can sing it after hearing it once.","t":"這首歌的旋律非常簡單,所以連小孩子聽一次就會唱。"},{"w":"harmony","p":"n.","d":"pleasant musical notes sung or played together","c":"和聲","s":"The four singers practised their harmony for hours, and their voices finally sounded like one beautiful voice.","t":"四位歌手練習和聲好幾個小時,他們的聲音終於聽起來像一個美麗的聲音。"},{"w":"lyrics","p":"n.","d":"the words of a song","c":"歌詞","s":"I love the tune, but I cannot understand the lyrics, so I looked them up online and translated them.","t":"我喜歡這個曲調,但聽不懂歌詞,所以我上網查了並把它們翻譯出來。"},{"w":"symphony","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of music for an orchestra","c":"交響曲","s":"Beethoven wrote his ninth symphony when he was almost completely deaf, and it is still played all over the world.","t":"貝多芬在幾乎全聾時寫下他的第九號交響曲,至今仍在世界各地演奏。"},{"w":"concert","p":"n.","d":"a musical performance in front of an audience","c":"音樂會;演唱會","s":"Thousands of fans waited outside the stadium all day, because the concert was the band's last in Taiwan.","t":"數千名粉絲整天在體育場外等待,因為這場演唱會是樂團在台灣的最後一場。"},{"w":"musician","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays or writes music","c":"音樂家","s":"The street musician played the violin every evening near the station, and many commuters stopped to listen on their way home.","t":"這位街頭音樂家每晚在車站附近拉小提琴,許多通勤族在回家途中停下來聆聽。"},{"w":"instrument","p":"n.","d":"an object such as a piano or guitar used to make music","c":"樂器","s":"Learning a musical instrument takes years of practice, but it can also improve your memory and patience.","t":"學習一種樂器需要多年練習,但它也能改善你的記憶力和耐心。"},{"w":"opera","p":"n.","d":"a play in which the words are sung with an orchestra","c":"歌劇","s":"Taiwanese opera is performed on outdoor stages near temples, and the actors wear colourful costumes and heavy make-up.","t":"台灣歌仔戲在廟宇附近的戶外舞台演出,演員穿著色彩繽紛的戲服、畫著濃妝。"},{"w":"musical","p":"n.","d":"a play or film with many songs and dances","c":"音樂劇","s":"We saw a Broadway musical in New York, and I could not stop singing its songs for weeks after the trip.","t":"我們在紐約看了一齣百老匯音樂劇,旅行結束後好幾週我都忍不住哼唱裡面的歌。"},{"w":"applause","p":"n.","d":"the sound of people clapping","c":"掌聲","s":"The applause continued for five minutes after the show ended, so the actors came back on stage three times.","t":"演出結束後掌聲持續了五分鐘,所以演員們回到台上謝幕了三次。"},{"w":"standing ovation","p":"n.phr.","d":"when an audience stands up to clap for a long time","c":"起立鼓掌","s":"The old pianist received a standing ovation after her last concert, and she bowed with tears in her eyes.","t":"這位年邁的鋼琴家在最後一場音樂會後獲得全場起立鼓掌,她眼含淚水鞠躬致意。"},{"w":"encore","p":"n.","d":"an extra song performed because the audience asks for it","c":"安可曲","s":"The crowd shouted for an encore, so the band came back and played their most famous song once more.","t":"觀眾大喊要安可曲,所以樂團回到台上再演奏了一次他們最有名的歌。"},{"w":"premiere","p":"n.","d":"the first public performance of a film or play","c":"首映;首演","s":"The actors walked on the red carpet at the film's premiere, while fans screamed and took photos behind the barriers.","t":"演員們在電影首映會上走紅毯,而粉絲們在圍欄後尖叫拍照。"},{"w":"busker","p":"n.","d":"a person who performs music in the street for money","c":"街頭藝人","s":"A talented busker was singing outside the department store, and people dropped coins into his guitar case.","t":"一位有才華的街頭藝人在百貨公司外唱歌,人們把硬幣丟進他的吉他盒裡。"},{"w":"costume","p":"n.","d":"clothes worn by actors in a show","c":"戲服","s":"The costume for the queen took two months to make, because every flower on the dress was sewn by hand.","t":"女王的戲服花了兩個月才完成,因為裙子上的每一朵花都是手工縫製的。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (admire – dabble)","cards":[{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to look at something with pleasure and respect","c":"欣賞;讚嘆","s":"We stopped to admire the huge mural for a few minutes, and then we took photos of it for our class project.","t":"我們停下來欣賞這幅巨大的壁畫幾分鐘,然後為班級報告拍了照片。"},{"w":"applaud","p":"v.","d":"to clap or to praise someone's action","c":"鼓掌;讚揚","s":"The audience began to applaud before the music finished, so the conductor turned around and smiled.","t":"音樂還沒結束觀眾就開始鼓掌,所以指揮轉過身來微笑。"},{"w":"astonish","p":"v.","d":"to surprise someone very much","c":"使驚訝","s":"The young girl's paintings astonish the judges, because nobody expected such skill from a ten-year-old.","t":"這位小女孩的畫作讓評審大為驚訝,因為沒人預料到一個十歲孩子有如此技巧。"},{"w":"captivate","p":"v.","d":"to hold someone's attention completely","c":"吸引;迷住","s":"The puppet show managed to captivate the noisy children, and the room became completely quiet within a minute.","t":"這場木偶戲成功吸引住吵鬧的孩子們,一分鐘內整個房間就變得鴉雀無聲。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to show that an event or person is important","c":"頌揚;慶祝","s":"The festival aims to celebrate local artists, so all the paintings on show were made by people from the village.","t":"這個藝術節旨在頌揚在地藝術家,所以所有展出的畫作都是村民創作的。"},{"w":"cherish","p":"v.","d":"to love and care for something very much","c":"珍惜;珍愛","s":"My mother still cherish the clay bowl I made in kindergarten, although it is uneven and slightly broken.","t":"我媽媽至今仍珍惜我幼稚園時做的陶碗,雖然它歪歪的又有點破損。"},{"w":"deconstruct","p":"v.","d":"to break an idea or object into parts to understand it","c":"解構","s":"In art history class, we deconstruct famous paintings by looking at their colours, shapes and hidden symbols one by one.","t":"在藝術史課上,我們透過逐一觀察顏色、形狀和隱藏的象徵來解構名畫。"},{"w":"delight","p":"v.","d":"to give someone great pleasure","c":"使高興;使欣喜","s":"The magician's tricks delight the children at the party, and they begged him to perform again.","t":"魔術師的把戲讓派對上的孩子們很開心,他們央求他再表演一次。"},{"w":"disapprove","p":"v.","d":"to think something is bad or wrong","c":"不贊成","s":"My parents disapprove of my plan to study art, because they think artists cannot earn enough money.","t":"我爸媽不贊成我念藝術的計畫,因為他們認為藝術家賺不了足夠的錢。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to examine or try out something in order to learn about it","c":"探索","s":"In her new paintings she wants to explore the feeling of loneliness, so many of them show empty streets at night.","t":"在她的新畫作中,她想探索孤獨的感受,所以許多作品描繪夜晚空蕩的街道。"},{"w":"fascinate","p":"v.","d":"to interest someone very much","c":"使著迷","s":"Old maps have always fascinate my brother, and he spends hours studying the strange sea monsters drawn on them.","t":"古地圖一向讓我哥哥著迷,他會花好幾個小時研究上面畫的奇怪海怪。"},{"w":"idolise","p":"v.","d":"to admire someone too much","c":"崇拜;偶像化","s":"Many teenagers idolise pop stars, but they often know little about the hard work behind the shows.","t":"許多青少年崇拜流行歌星,但他們往往對演出背後的辛苦所知甚少。"},{"w":"immerse","p":"v.","d":"to become completely involved in something","c":"沉浸","s":"When she paints, she likes to immerse herself in the work, so she turns off her phone for the whole afternoon.","t":"她畫畫時喜歡讓自己完全沉浸其中,所以她整個下午都會關掉手機。"},{"w":"liberate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone free","c":"解放","s":"Photography helped liberate painters from simply copying reality, so they began to experiment with colour and shape.","t":"攝影幫助解放畫家,使他們不必只是複製現實,於是他們開始實驗色彩與形狀。"},{"w":"mesmerise","p":"v.","d":"to hold someone's attention so they cannot look away","c":"使入迷","s":"The dancer's slow movements seemed to mesmerise the crowd, and nobody even took out a phone during the show.","t":"舞者緩慢的動作似乎讓觀眾入迷,表演期間甚至沒有人拿出手機。"},{"w":"personify","p":"v.","d":"to give human qualities to an object or idea","c":"擬人化","s":"Many fairy tales personify the wind and the moon, so children imagine that nature can talk and feel.","t":"許多童話把風和月亮擬人化,所以孩子們想像大自然會說話、有感覺。"},{"w":"reinterpret","p":"v.","d":"to explain or perform something in a new way","c":"重新詮釋","s":"The young director decided to reinterpret the old Chinese legend, and she set the story in modern Taipei.","t":"這位年輕導演決定重新詮釋這個中國古老傳說,並把故事背景設在現代台北。"},{"w":"reimagine","p":"v.","d":"to think about something again in a new way","c":"重新構想","s":"The designers wanted to reimagine the old factory as an art centre, so they kept the brick walls but added glass roofs.","t":"設計師們想把舊工廠重新構想成藝術中心,所以保留了磚牆但加上玻璃屋頂。"},{"w":"popularise","p":"v.","d":"to make something liked by many people","c":"使普及","s":"Television shows helped popularise cooking as a hobby, and now many young people share their recipes online.","t":"電視節目幫助普及了烹飪這項嗜好,現在許多年輕人在網路上分享食譜。"},{"w":"democratise","p":"v.","d":"to make something available to everyone","c":"使大眾化","s":"Smartphones have democratise photography, because almost everyone now carries a good camera in their pocket.","t":"智慧型手機讓攝影大眾化了,因為現在幾乎人人口袋裡都有一台好相機。"},{"w":"innovate","p":"v.","d":"to introduce new ideas or methods","c":"創新","s":"Artists who refuse to innovate may lose their audience, because people want to see something fresh.","t":"拒絕創新的藝術家可能會失去觀眾,因為人們想看到新鮮的東西。"},{"w":"borrow","p":"v.","d":"to take and use an idea from another person or culture","c":"借用","s":"Many Western artists borrow ideas from Japanese prints in the 1800s, and you can see this in their bold, flat colours.","t":"1800年代許多西方藝術家借用了日本版畫的構想,你可以從他們大膽平塗的色彩中看出這點。"},{"w":"crystallise","p":"v.","d":"to make an idea clear and definite","c":"使具體化;使明確","s":"Talking with my teacher helped crystallise my ideas, so I finally knew what my final project would be about.","t":"和老師談話幫助我把想法具體化,所以我終於知道期末作品要做什麼了。"},{"w":"typify","p":"v.","d":"to be a typical example of something","c":"是…的典型","s":"Bright colours and bold lines typify his early work, while his later paintings are much darker.","t":"鮮豔的色彩和大膽的線條是他早期作品的典型特徵,而他晚期的畫作則陰暗許多。"},{"w":"dabble","p":"v.","d":"to try an activity without being serious about it","c":"涉獵;玩票","s":"My father likes to dabble in painting at weekends, but he says he will never show his work to anyone.","t":"我爸爸週末喜歡玩票畫畫,但他說他絕不會把作品給任何人看。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (outshine – craftsmanship)","cards":[{"w":"outshine","p":"v.","d":"to be much better than others","c":"勝過;比…出色","s":"The young actor managed to outshine the famous stars in the film, so many critics praised his performance.","t":"這位年輕演員在片中勝過了那些知名明星,所以許多影評人稱讚他的演出。"},{"w":"redeem","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem less bad","c":"彌補;挽回","s":"The film's story is weak, but the beautiful music helps redeem it, so I still enjoyed watching it.","t":"這部電影的劇情很弱,但優美的配樂幫忙彌補了缺點,所以我還是看得很開心。"},{"w":"rekindle","p":"v.","d":"to make a feeling active again","c":"重新燃起","s":"Visiting the art museum helped rekindle my interest in drawing, so I bought a new sketchbook on the way home.","t":"參觀美術館重新燃起我對畫畫的興趣,所以我在回家路上買了一本新的素描本。"},{"w":"enliven","p":"v.","d":"to make something more lively and interesting","c":"使有生氣","s":"Colourful murals enliven the grey walls of the old market, and more young people now visit it at weekends.","t":"色彩繽紛的壁畫讓老市場灰色的牆面有了生氣,現在週末有更多年輕人來逛。"},{"w":"ridicule","p":"v.","d":"to laugh at someone in an unkind way","c":"嘲笑","s":"Critics ridicule the Impressionists at first, but today their paintings are among the most expensive in the world.","t":"評論家起初嘲笑印象派畫家,但如今他們的畫作是世上最昂貴的作品之一。"},{"w":"scorn","p":"v.","d":"to show that you think something is worthless","c":"輕蔑;鄙視","s":"Some traditional painters scorn digital art, but young artists believe a tablet is just another kind of brush.","t":"有些傳統畫家鄙視數位藝術,但年輕藝術家認為平板只是另一種畫筆。"},{"w":"mock","p":"v.","d":"to laugh at someone and make them look silly","c":"嘲弄","s":"Classmates used to mock his strange drawings, but now he is a successful illustrator with thousands of fans.","t":"同學以前常嘲弄他奇怪的畫,但現在他是擁有數千名粉絲的成功插畫家。"},{"w":"satirise","p":"v.","d":"to use humour to criticise people or ideas","c":"諷刺","s":"The comedy show likes to satirise politicians, so some leaders have tried to stop it from being broadcast.","t":"這個喜劇節目喜歡諷刺政治人物,所以有些領導人曾試圖阻止它播出。"},{"w":"persevere","p":"v.","d":"to keep trying although it is difficult","c":"堅持不懈","s":"Learning the violin was very hard at first, but she decided to persevere, and now she plays in a famous orchestra.","t":"學小提琴一開始非常困難,但她決定堅持不懈,現在她在一個知名管弦樂團演奏。"},{"w":"recreate","p":"v.","d":"to make something exist again or copy it","c":"重現","s":"The students tried to recreate the famous painting using only coloured rice, and the result looked surprisingly good.","t":"學生們試著只用彩色米粒重現那幅名畫,結果看起來出奇地好。"},{"w":"unsettle","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel worried or uncomfortable","c":"使不安","s":"The dark film is designed to unsettle viewers, so the music becomes louder whenever the camera moves slowly.","t":"這部黑暗電影的設計就是要讓觀眾不安,所以每當鏡頭緩慢移動時音樂就會變大聲。"},{"w":"intrigue","p":"v.","d":"to make someone very interested and curious","c":"引起好奇","s":"The strange title of the exhibition intrigue me, so I went inside although I had planned to go shopping.","t":"展覽奇特的名稱引起我的好奇,所以雖然我原本打算去逛街,還是走了進去。"},{"w":"enchant","p":"v.","d":"to charm and delight someone","c":"使陶醉;迷住","s":"The old fairy-tale illustrations enchant readers of every age, and the book has been printed again and again.","t":"這些古老的童話插畫迷住了各個年齡層的讀者,這本書也一再重印。"},{"w":"dazzle","p":"v.","d":"to impress someone greatly with skill or beauty","c":"使驚豔;使目眩","s":"The fireworks show dazzle the crowd by the river, and everyone looked up at the sky with their mouths open.","t":"煙火秀讓河邊的人群驚豔不已,每個人都張大嘴巴仰望天空。"},{"w":"transfix","p":"v.","d":"to make someone unable to move because of shock or interest","c":"使呆住","s":"The huge whale sculpture seemed to transfix the children, and they stood under it without saying a word.","t":"那座巨大的鯨魚雕塑似乎讓孩子們看呆了,他們一語不發地站在它下面。"},{"w":"underfund","p":"v.","d":"to give too little money to something","c":"資金不足","s":"The government continues to underfund the arts, so many small theatres have closed in recent years.","t":"政府持續對藝術投入不足的資金,所以近年來許多小劇場都關門了。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone confidence or support to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"Good teachers encourage students to try new materials, and they do not punish them for messy experiments.","t":"好老師會鼓勵學生嘗試新素材,而且不會因為實驗弄得亂七八糟而處罰他們。"},{"w":"unlock","p":"v.","d":"to release or make something available","c":"釋放;開啟","s":"Music can unlock old memories in people with poor memory, so some care homes play songs from the 1960s.","t":"音樂能為記憶力不好的人開啟舊回憶,所以有些安養院會播放1960年代的歌曲。"},{"w":"polish","p":"v.","d":"to improve something by making small changes","c":"潤飾;改進","s":"The singer spent a week trying to polish her performance, but she still felt nervous before the competition.","t":"這位歌手花了一週試圖潤飾她的演出,但比賽前她仍然感到緊張。"},{"w":"abstraction","p":"n.","d":"art that does not show real objects","c":"抽象","s":"Her early paintings show real people, but later she moved towards pure abstraction, using only lines and colour.","t":"她早期的畫作描繪真實人物,但後來轉向純粹的抽象,只使用線條和色彩。"},{"w":"admiration","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great respect and approval","c":"欽佩;讚賞","s":"I have great admiration for street artists, because they work in the heat and rain but rarely receive any credit.","t":"我非常欽佩街頭藝術家,因為他們在炎熱和雨中工作,卻很少得到認可。"},{"w":"awe","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great respect mixed with wonder","c":"敬畏;驚嘆","s":"We stood in awe in front of the giant Buddha statue, because it was much larger than we had imagined.","t":"我們滿懷敬畏地站在巨大的佛像前,因為它比我們想像的大得多。"},{"w":"canon","p":"n.","d":"the group of works seen as the most important","c":"經典作品;正典","s":"Women artists were often left out of the art canon, so museums are now trying to show more of their work.","t":"女性藝術家常被排除在藝術經典作品之外,所以博物館現在正努力展出更多她們的作品。"},{"w":"contemplation","p":"n.","d":"quiet, careful thinking about something","c":"沉思","s":"The quiet garden was designed for contemplation, so visitors are asked to turn off their phones and speak softly.","t":"這座寧靜的庭園是為沉思而設計的,所以遊客被要求關掉手機並輕聲說話。"},{"w":"craftsmanship","p":"n.","d":"skill in making things by hand","c":"工藝技術;手藝","s":"The craftsmanship of this wooden temple door is amazing, because no nails were used to hold it together.","t":"這扇木製廟門的工藝技術令人驚嘆,因為完全沒有使用釘子來固定。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (discernment – sincerity)","cards":[{"w":"discernment","p":"n.","d":"the ability to judge what is good","c":"鑑賞力;辨別力","s":"Collectors need discernment to choose valuable paintings, because many attractive works lose their value over time.","t":"收藏家需要鑑賞力來挑選有價值的畫作,因為許多吸引人的作品會隨時間貶值。"},{"w":"elegance","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being graceful and stylish","c":"優雅","s":"The dancer moved with great elegance, so the audience hardly noticed how difficult the steps were.","t":"這位舞者的動作極為優雅,所以觀眾幾乎沒察覺舞步有多困難。"},{"w":"embellishment","p":"n.","d":"a decoration added to make something more attractive","c":"裝飾;潤色","s":"The old palace door has gold embellishment on every corner, but the simple wooden centre is actually the oldest part.","t":"這扇古老宮殿大門的每個角落都有金色裝飾,但樸素的木製中央部分其實是最古老的。"},{"w":"enthusiast","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very interested in an activity","c":"愛好者;熱衷者","s":"My uncle is a jazz enthusiast, and he has collected more than two thousand old records since he was a teenager.","t":"我叔叔是爵士樂愛好者,他從青少年時期就收集了兩千多張老唱片。"},{"w":"esteem","p":"n.","d":"respect and admiration","c":"尊敬;敬重","s":"The old calligrapher is held in high esteem in his town, so people ask him to write couplets for every festival.","t":"這位老書法家在鎮上備受敬重,所以每逢節慶大家都請他寫春聯。"},{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"showing feelings or ideas through words or art","c":"表達","s":"Poetry was her main form of expression, because she found it difficult to talk about her feelings with others.","t":"詩是她主要的表達方式,因為她發現很難和別人談論自己的感受。"},{"w":"fascination","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest","c":"著迷","s":"His fascination with insects began in childhood, and later he became famous for his detailed drawings of butterflies.","t":"他對昆蟲的著迷從童年就開始了,後來他以精細的蝴蝶素描而聞名。"},{"w":"iconography","p":"n.","d":"the symbols used in a type of art and their meanings","c":"圖像學;象徵圖像","s":"Temple iconography is full of meaning, because each animal and colour on the roof represents a different blessing.","t":"廟宇的象徵圖像充滿意義,因為屋頂上的每種動物和顏色都代表不同的祝福。"},{"w":"ideal","p":"n.","d":"a perfect idea or standard you want to reach","c":"理想","s":"Ancient Greek statues show an ideal of beauty, but real people rarely looked so perfect.","t":"古希臘雕像展現了一種美的理想,但真實的人很少看起來那麼完美。"},{"w":"imagery","p":"n.","d":"pictures or descriptions that create images in the mind","c":"意象","s":"The poem uses rich imagery of the sea, so readers can almost hear the waves when they read it aloud.","t":"這首詩運用了豐富的海洋意象,所以讀者朗讀時幾乎能聽見浪聲。"},{"w":"impression","p":"n.","d":"the feeling or idea you get from something","c":"印象","s":"My first impression of the gallery was not good, but the guide's stories changed my mind completely.","t":"我對這家畫廊的第一印象不太好,但導覽員的故事完全改變了我的想法。"},{"w":"intellect","p":"n.","d":"the ability to think and understand ideas","c":"智力;才智","s":"His paintings appeal to the intellect more than the heart, so some viewers find them clever but cold.","t":"他的畫作訴諸理智多於情感,所以有些觀眾覺得它們聰明卻冷漠。"},{"w":"juxtaposition","p":"n.","d":"placing two different things side by side","c":"並置;對比","s":"The juxtaposition of old temples and glass towers makes the city photos interesting, because it shows the past and future together.","t":"古廟與玻璃高樓的並置讓這些城市照片很有趣,因為它同時呈現過去與未來。"},{"w":"magnificence","p":"n.","d":"great beauty and impressive size","c":"壯麗;宏偉","s":"Photos cannot show the magnificence of the cathedral ceiling, so you really need to see it with your own eyes.","t":"照片無法呈現大教堂天花板的壯麗,所以你真的需要親眼去看看。"},{"w":"obscurity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being unknown","c":"默默無聞","s":"The painter lived in obscurity for most of his life, and only a few friends bought his paintings.","t":"這位畫家大半生都默默無聞,只有幾位朋友買過他的畫。"},{"w":"patronage","p":"n.","d":"money and support given to artists by a rich person","c":"贊助","s":"Thanks to the patronage of wealthy families, many Renaissance artists could work without worrying about food and rent.","t":"由於富裕家族的贊助,許多文藝復興時期的藝術家能夠工作而不必擔心吃住問題。"},{"w":"portrayal","p":"n.","d":"the way someone or something is shown in art","c":"描繪;刻畫","s":"The film's portrayal of a teenage girl feels very real, because the director interviewed hundreds of students.","t":"這部電影對少女的刻畫感覺非常真實,因為導演訪問了數百名學生。"},{"w":"prestige","p":"n.","d":"respect that comes from success or importance","c":"聲望","s":"Winning the award brought great prestige to the small design company, and big clients soon began to call.","t":"贏得這個獎為這家小設計公司帶來極高的聲望,大客戶很快就開始打電話來了。"},{"w":"rendition","p":"n.","d":"a performance of a song or piece of music","c":"演繹;演唱","s":"Her rendition of the old folk song was so beautiful that my grandmother started to sing along quietly.","t":"她對那首老民謠的演繹美極了,我奶奶也開始輕聲跟著唱。"},{"w":"renown","p":"n.","d":"the state of being famous","c":"名聲;聲望","s":"The ceramic artist gained international renown after her work appeared in a London museum, and her prices rose sharply.","t":"這位陶藝家的作品在倫敦一家博物館展出後,她獲得了國際聲望,作品價格也大幅上漲。"},{"w":"reproduction","p":"n.","d":"a copy of a work of art","c":"複製品","s":"The painting in our classroom is only a cheap reproduction, but it still helps us learn about the original.","t":"我們教室裡的畫只是一幅便宜的複製品,但它仍幫助我們認識原作。"},{"w":"resonance","p":"n.","d":"a special meaning or importance for someone","c":"共鳴","s":"The song has special resonance for older Taiwanese listeners, because it reminds them of their hometowns.","t":"這首歌對年長的台灣聽眾有特別的共鳴,因為它讓他們想起家鄉。"},{"w":"revival","p":"n.","d":"a time when something becomes popular again","c":"復興;重新流行","s":"There has been a revival of interest in film cameras, and many teenagers now use them to take holiday photos.","t":"人們對底片相機的興趣重新流行起來,現在許多青少年用它們拍度假照片。"},{"w":"sensibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand and enjoy art or feelings","c":"感受力;藝術感","s":"The young poet shows a rare sensibility to nature, and her short poems about rain are loved by many readers.","t":"這位年輕詩人展現了對自然罕見的感受力,她寫雨的短詩深受許多讀者喜愛。"},{"w":"sincerity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being honest and true in feelings","c":"真誠","s":"The audience could feel the sincerity in his songs, because he wrote them about his own difficult childhood.","t":"觀眾能感受到他歌曲中的真誠,因為他寫的是自己艱辛的童年。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (sophistication – uniqueness)","cards":[{"w":"sophistication","p":"n.","d":"a high level of skill and complexity","c":"精緻;成熟老練","s":"The sophistication of the young designer's work surprised everyone, because she had never studied at an art school.","t":"這位年輕設計師作品的成熟老練讓所有人驚訝,因為她從未在藝術學校念過書。"},{"w":"symbolism","p":"n.","d":"the use of objects or colours to represent ideas","c":"象徵手法","s":"The painting is full of symbolism, and the broken clock in the corner represents the end of the artist's youth.","t":"這幅畫充滿象徵手法,角落那座壞掉的時鐘代表藝術家青春的結束。"},{"w":"vibrancy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being bright, lively and exciting","c":"活力;鮮明","s":"The vibrancy of the night market inspired her photos, because she loved the colours, noise and steam everywhere.","t":"夜市的活力啟發了她的攝影作品,因為她熱愛那裡無處不在的色彩、喧鬧與蒸氣。"},{"w":"virtuosity","p":"n.","d":"very great skill in music or art","c":"精湛技藝","s":"The violinist played with such virtuosity that the audience stood up and cheered before the last note ended.","t":"這位小提琴家的演奏技藝如此精湛,觀眾在最後一個音結束前就起立歡呼。"},{"w":"audacity","p":"n.","d":"brave or rude confidence to do something shocking","c":"膽量;大膽","s":"Critics were shocked by the audacity of the young artist, because she hung an ordinary bicycle in the national gallery.","t":"評論家對這位年輕藝術家的大膽感到震驚,因為她把一輛普通的腳踏車掛在國家美術館裡。"},{"w":"excellence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being extremely good","c":"卓越","s":"The award recognises excellence in film-making, and this year it went to a documentary about mountain villages.","t":"這個獎項表彰電影製作的卓越成就,今年頒給了一部關於山村的紀錄片。"},{"w":"finesse","p":"n.","d":"great skill and delicate care","c":"精巧;手法細膩","s":"The chef decorates every cake with finesse, so each one looks like a small work of art.","t":"這位甜點師以細膩的手法裝飾每個蛋糕,所以每個都像一件小小的藝術品。"},{"w":"flamboyance","p":"n.","d":"a very confident, colourful and showy style","c":"浮誇;張揚","s":"The singer is famous for his flamboyance, and he often appears on stage in gold suits and huge feathered hats.","t":"這位歌手以張揚聞名,他常穿著金色西裝、戴著巨大的羽毛帽登台。"},{"w":"grace","p":"n.","d":"a smooth and attractive way of moving","c":"優美;優雅","s":"The ballerina crossed the stage with great grace, and she seemed to float above the floor like a feather.","t":"這位芭蕾舞者以極為優美的姿態穿越舞台,彷彿羽毛般飄浮在地板上方。"},{"w":"humility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of not thinking you are better than others","c":"謙遜","s":"Despite his fame, the old master spoke with great humility, and he thanked his students for teaching him new ideas.","t":"儘管名聞遐邇,這位老大師說話時非常謙遜,還感謝學生教了他新想法。"},{"w":"irony","p":"n.","d":"a situation that is the opposite of what you expect","c":"諷刺","s":"The irony is that the painter died poor, while his paintings now sell for millions of dollars.","t":"諷刺的是,這位畫家死時一貧如洗,而他的畫作如今卻以數百萬美元售出。"},{"w":"legitimacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being accepted as real or fair","c":"正當性;合法地位","s":"Street art has gained more legitimacy in recent years, and some cities now invite artists to paint public walls.","t":"近年來街頭藝術獲得更多正當性,有些城市現在還邀請藝術家彩繪公共牆面。"},{"w":"mastery","p":"n.","d":"great skill or knowledge of something","c":"精通;熟練掌握","s":"His mastery of light and shadow makes his paintings look almost real, and visitors often try to touch them.","t":"他對光影的精通讓他的畫看起來幾乎是真的,參觀者常想伸手去摸。"},{"w":"mediocrity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being only average and not very good","c":"平庸","s":"The director refused to accept mediocrity, so the actors had to repeat each scene until it was perfect.","t":"導演拒絕接受平庸,所以演員們必須重複每一場戲直到完美為止。"},{"w":"melancholy","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of quiet sadness","c":"憂鬱;惆悵","s":"There is a deep melancholy in his paintings of empty beaches, because he painted them after his wife passed away.","t":"他筆下空曠海灘的畫作中有一種深沉的憂鬱,因為那是他在妻子過世後畫的。"},{"w":"objectivity","p":"n.","d":"judging fairly without personal feelings","c":"客觀性","s":"It is hard to judge art with complete objectivity, because each person brings different feelings and memories to a painting.","t":"要完全客觀地評判藝術很難,因為每個人面對畫作時都帶著不同的感受和記憶。"},{"w":"pastiche","p":"n.","d":"a work that copies the style of other artists","c":"仿作;拼湊模仿之作","s":"The film is a pastiche of old Hollywood musicals, so fans of classic movies will recognise many of the scenes.","t":"這部電影是老好萊塢歌舞片的仿作,所以經典電影迷會認出許多場景。"},{"w":"pluralism","p":"n.","d":"the acceptance of many different styles or beliefs","c":"多元並存","s":"Today's art world is marked by pluralism, because no single style is more important than the others.","t":"當今藝術界的特色是多元並存,因為沒有任何單一風格比其他風格更重要。"},{"w":"poise","p":"n.","d":"a calm, confident way of behaving","c":"沉著;泰然自若","s":"Although she was only twelve, the pianist played with great poise, and she did not seem nervous at all.","t":"雖然這位鋼琴家只有十二歲,她演奏時卻非常沉著,一點也不顯得緊張。"},{"w":"reinvention","p":"n.","d":"changing yourself or something completely","c":"重新塑造;改頭換面","s":"The singer is famous for constant reinvention, and every new album comes with a different look and sound.","t":"這位歌手以不斷改頭換面聞名,每張新專輯都有不同的造型和曲風。"},{"w":"reverence","p":"n.","d":"deep respect","c":"崇敬","s":"Visitors speak with reverence inside the old temple, and they bow before the carved statues of the gods.","t":"參觀者在古廟內帶著崇敬輕聲說話,並在神明雕像前鞠躬。"},{"w":"solitude","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone, often happily","c":"獨處;孤獨","s":"Many writers need solitude to work, so they rent quiet rooms in the mountains far from their families.","t":"許多作家需要獨處才能工作,所以他們會在遠離家人的山上租安靜的房間。"},{"w":"transcendence","p":"n.","d":"going beyond ordinary experience","c":"超越;超凡","s":"Some people feel a sense of transcendence when they listen to great music, as if their worries suddenly disappear.","t":"有些人聆聽偉大的音樂時會感到一種超凡的感受,彷彿煩惱突然消失了。"},{"w":"triumph","p":"n.","d":"a great success","c":"巨大成功;勝利","s":"The opening night was a triumph, and the young director received flowers from the whole cast after the show.","t":"首演之夜大獲成功,演出後年輕導演收到全體演員送的花。"},{"w":"uniqueness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being the only one of its kind","c":"獨特性","s":"The uniqueness of each handmade cup makes it special, because no two cups have exactly the same shape.","t":"每個手工杯子的獨特性使它與眾不同,因為沒有兩個杯子的形狀完全相同。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (versatility – enigmatic)","cards":[{"w":"versatility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do many different things well","c":"多才多藝;多樣性","s":"The actor is famous for his versatility, and he can play a funny teacher one year and a cruel king the next.","t":"這位演員以多才多藝聞名,他今年能演搞笑老師,明年又能演殘暴的國王。"},{"w":"whimsy","p":"n.","d":"playful, unusual humour","c":"奇想;異想天開","s":"The children's book is full of whimsy, so cats ride bicycles and teapots dance on the kitchen table.","t":"這本童書充滿奇想,所以貓會騎腳踏車,茶壺會在廚房餐桌上跳舞。"},{"w":"wit","p":"n.","d":"the ability to say clever and funny things","c":"機智;風趣","s":"The writer's wit made the serious topic easy to read, and readers laughed while they learned about history.","t":"作者的風趣讓嚴肅的主題變得好讀,讀者一邊學歷史一邊大笑。"},{"w":"zest","p":"n.","d":"great energy and enthusiasm","c":"熱情;興致","s":"At eighty, the painter still works with great zest, and she gets up at five every morning to paint.","t":"八十歲的這位畫家仍然充滿熱情地工作,她每天早上五點起床畫畫。"},{"w":"elitism","p":"n.","d":"the belief that only a small group deserves the best things","c":"菁英主義","s":"Some people accuse classical music of elitism, because concert tickets are expensive and the dress code feels strict.","t":"有些人指責古典音樂有菁英主義之嫌,因為音樂會票價昂貴,服裝規定也讓人覺得嚴格。"},{"w":"exclusivity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being available only to a few people","c":"獨佔性;排他性","s":"The gallery sells limited prints to create a sense of exclusivity, so collectors feel lucky when they get one.","t":"這家畫廊販售限量版畫來營造獨佔性,所以收藏家買到時會覺得很幸運。"},{"w":"provocation","p":"n.","d":"an action that makes people angry or react","c":"挑釁","s":"The artist's broken toilet was a deliberate provocation, because he wanted people to argue about what art means.","t":"這位藝術家的破馬桶作品是刻意的挑釁,因為他想讓人們爭論藝術的意義。"},{"w":"appropriation","p":"n.","d":"taking something from another person or culture and using it","c":"挪用","s":"Some fashion designers have been criticised for appropriation of traditional patterns, because they did not ask local communities first.","t":"有些時裝設計師因挪用傳統圖騰而受到批評,因為他們事先沒有徵詢當地社群。"},{"w":"inclusivity","p":"n.","d":"including all kinds of people","c":"包容性","s":"The museum is working on inclusivity, so it now offers sign language tours and touchable sculptures for blind visitors.","t":"這間博物館正致力於包容性,所以現在提供手語導覽和可供視障者觸摸的雕塑。"},{"w":"funding","p":"n.","d":"money given for a particular purpose","c":"資金;經費","s":"The theatre lost its government funding last year, so it had to ask local businesses for help.","t":"這家劇院去年失去了政府經費,所以必須向在地企業求助。"},{"w":"philanthropy","p":"n.","d":"giving money to help others","c":"慈善事業","s":"Her philanthropy has helped many young musicians, because she pays for their lessons and buys them good instruments.","t":"她的慈善事業幫助了許多年輕音樂家,因為她為他們支付課程費用並買好樂器給他們。"},{"w":"luminary","p":"n.","d":"a famous and respected person in a field","c":"傑出人物;泰斗","s":"The festival invited several luminary of world cinema, and students queued for hours to hear them speak.","t":"影展邀請了數位世界電影界的泰斗,學生們排隊好幾個小時聽他們演講。"},{"w":"devotee","p":"n.","d":"a person who loves an activity very much","c":"愛好者;熱衷者","s":"As a devotee of Taiwanese puppet theatre, my uncle watches every performance at the temple festival.","t":"身為台灣布袋戲的熱衷者,我叔叔看遍廟會上的每一場演出。"},{"w":"aficionado","p":"n.","d":"a person who knows and loves a subject well","c":"行家;狂熱愛好者","s":"Every film aficionado in the city came to see the old movie, because it had not been shown for forty years.","t":"城裡每位電影行家都來看這部老電影,因為它已經四十年沒有放映了。"},{"w":"maestro","p":"n.","d":"a great musician or conductor","c":"大師;名指揮","s":"The old maestro conducted the orchestra without any notes, and the young musicians followed every movement of his hands.","t":"這位老大師不看樂譜指揮管弦樂團,年輕樂手們緊隨他手上的每一個動作。"},{"w":"acclaimed","p":"adj.","d":"praised by many people","c":"廣受讚譽的","s":"The acclaimed director spoke to our class about her films, and she told us to watch people carefully on buses.","t":"這位廣受讚譽的導演到我們班上談她的電影,她告訴我們要在公車上仔細觀察人們。"},{"w":"accomplished","p":"adj.","d":"very skilled at something","c":"技藝精湛的;有造詣的","s":"My piano teacher is an accomplished musician, but she is very patient with beginners like me.","t":"我的鋼琴老師是一位技藝精湛的音樂家,但她對像我這樣的初學者非常有耐心。"},{"w":"appealing","p":"adj.","d":"attractive or interesting","c":"吸引人的","s":"The bright cover makes the book appealing to children, so it sells well in bookshops near primary schools.","t":"鮮豔的封面讓這本書對孩子很吸引人,所以它在國小附近的書店賣得很好。"},{"w":"awe-inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel great respect and wonder","c":"令人敬畏的;令人驚嘆的","s":"The view from the top of the mountain was awe-inspiring, and several of us were too surprised to say anything.","t":"山頂的景色令人驚嘆,我們好幾個人驚訝得說不出話。"},{"w":"bold","p":"adj.","d":"strong and clear, or brave","c":"大膽的;醒目的","s":"The poster uses bold red letters, so people can read it easily from the other side of the street.","t":"這張海報使用醒目的紅色字體,所以人們從對街就能輕鬆看清。"},{"w":"breathtaking","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or surprising","c":"令人屏息的","s":"The dancers' final jump was breathtaking, and the whole theatre was silent for a second before everyone cheered.","t":"舞者最後一躍令人屏息,整座劇院安靜了一秒,接著所有人歡呼起來。"},{"w":"budding","p":"adj.","d":"starting to develop and showing promise","c":"嶄露頭角的;初露鋒芒的","s":"The summer camp is designed for budding artists, so most of the students are teenagers who have just begun painting.","t":"這個夏令營是為嶄露頭角的藝術家設計的,所以大多數學員是剛開始畫畫的青少年。"},{"w":"daring","p":"adj.","d":"brave and willing to take risks","c":"大膽的;勇於冒險的","s":"Her daring designs shocked the fashion world, but young people loved the unusual colours and shapes.","t":"她大膽的設計震驚時尚界,但年輕人很喜歡那些不尋常的色彩和造型。"},{"w":"decorative","p":"adj.","d":"made to look pretty","c":"裝飾性的","s":"The plates are purely decorative, so please do not put food on them or wash them in the dishwasher.","t":"這些盤子純屬裝飾性的,所以請不要在上面放食物或放進洗碗機清洗。"},{"w":"enigmatic","p":"adj.","d":"mysterious and hard to understand","c":"神秘的;令人費解的","s":"The woman in the painting has an enigmatic smile, and visitors still argue about whether she is happy or sad.","t":"畫中女子帶著神秘的微笑,參觀者至今仍爭論她是開心還是難過。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (evocative – superb)","cards":[{"w":"evocative","p":"adj.","d":"bringing strong memories or feelings to mind","c":"引起回憶的;喚起情感的","s":"The smell of the old bookshop was very evocative, and it reminded me of reading with my father as a child.","t":"舊書店的氣味非常喚起回憶,讓我想起小時候和爸爸一起閱讀的時光。"},{"w":"flawless","p":"adj.","d":"perfect, with no mistakes","c":"完美無瑕的","s":"The pianist gave a flawless performance, but she said afterwards that her hands were shaking the whole time.","t":"這位鋼琴家的演出完美無瑕,但她事後說她的手一直在發抖。"},{"w":"iconic","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and seen as a symbol","c":"具代表性的;標誌性的","s":"Taipei 101 is an iconic building, so it appears on many postcards, posters and souvenirs.","t":"台北101是一棟具代表性的建築,所以它出現在許多明信片、海報和紀念品上。"},{"w":"immortal","p":"adj.","d":"remembered for ever","c":"不朽的","s":"Shakespeare's plays seem immortal, because people around the world still perform them four hundred years later.","t":"莎士比亞的戲劇似乎是不朽的,因為四百年後世界各地的人們仍在演出。"},{"w":"inspirational","p":"adj.","d":"making people want to do something good","c":"激勵人心的","s":"The blind painter gave an inspirational talk at our school, and many students decided to try new hobbies afterwards.","t":"這位盲人畫家在我們學校發表了一場激勵人心的演講,之後許多學生決定嘗試新嗜好。"},{"w":"legendary","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and admired for a long time","c":"傳奇的","s":"The legendary guitarist played a free concert in the park, and fans travelled from other cities to see him.","t":"這位傳奇吉他手在公園舉辦免費音樂會,歌迷從其他城市遠道而來看他。"},{"w":"literary","p":"adj.","d":"relating to books, poems and writing","c":"文學的","s":"She won a literary prize for her first novel, and the book was soon translated into twelve languages.","t":"她以第一本小說贏得文學獎,這本書很快就被翻譯成十二種語言。"},{"w":"majestic","p":"adj.","d":"very beautiful, large and impressive","c":"雄偉的;莊嚴的","s":"The majestic mountains in the painting look calm and strong, while the tiny boat below seems lost.","t":"畫中雄偉的山脈看起來沉靜而堅毅,而下方的小船則顯得迷茫。"},{"w":"meaningful","p":"adj.","d":"important and having a clear purpose","c":"有意義的","s":"Making art with elderly people was a meaningful experience, because they shared stories about their lives as they painted.","t":"和長者一起創作藝術是一次有意義的經驗,因為他們邊畫邊分享自己的人生故事。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"worth remembering","c":"難忘的","s":"The concert on the beach was truly memorable, because the sun set behind the stage during the last song.","t":"海灘上的音樂會真的令人難忘,因為最後一首歌時太陽在舞台後方落下。"},{"w":"moving","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel strong emotions, especially sadness","c":"感人的","s":"The film about the old dog was so moving that I cried, and my friend had to give me a tissue.","t":"那部關於老狗的電影太感人了,我哭了,朋友只好遞給我一張面紙。"},{"w":"nostalgic","p":"adj.","d":"feeling happy and sad about the past","c":"懷舊的","s":"Old cartoon songs make my parents feel nostalgic, so they sing along whenever they hear them on the radio.","t":"老卡通歌曲讓我爸媽感到懷舊,所以每當在收音機聽到時他們都會跟著唱。"},{"w":"nuanced","p":"adj.","d":"showing small but important differences","c":"細膩的;有層次的","s":"The actor gave a nuanced performance, so the villain seemed both cruel and lonely at the same time.","t":"這位演員的演出非常細膩,所以反派角色同時顯得既殘忍又孤獨。"},{"w":"ornamental","p":"adj.","d":"used for decoration rather than use","c":"裝飾用的","s":"The garden has many ornamental stones, but the children use them as chairs during the summer festival.","t":"花園裡有許多裝飾用的石頭,但夏日節慶時孩子們把它們當椅子坐。"},{"w":"poetic","p":"adj.","d":"beautiful and full of feeling, like poetry","c":"詩意的","s":"The film has a poetic ending, and the last scene shows two old friends watching the rain in silence.","t":"這部電影有個富有詩意的結局,最後一幕是兩位老朋友默默看著雨。"},{"w":"radiant","p":"adj.","d":"bright and shining","c":"燦爛的;容光煥發的","s":"The bride looked radiant in her red dress, and the photographer said it was the easiest wedding he had ever photographed.","t":"新娘穿著紅色禮服容光煥發,攝影師說這是他拍過最輕鬆的婚禮。"},{"w":"refined","p":"adj.","d":"elegant and showing good taste","c":"精緻的;高雅的","s":"The tea house has a refined atmosphere, so customers speak quietly while they enjoy their tea.","t":"這間茶館有著高雅的氛圍,所以顧客品茶時都輕聲細語。"},{"w":"representational","p":"adj.","d":"showing things as they look in real life","c":"具象的","s":"Children usually start with representational drawings of houses and people, but later some of them try abstract shapes.","t":"孩子們通常從房子和人物的具象畫開始,但後來有些人會嘗試抽象形狀。"},{"w":"restrained","p":"adj.","d":"calm and controlled, not too strong","c":"克制的;含蓄的","s":"The actor gave a restrained performance, but his quiet sadness touched the audience more than loud crying could.","t":"這位演員的演出很克制,但他安靜的哀傷比大聲哭泣更打動觀眾。"},{"w":"rhythmic","p":"adj.","d":"having a regular repeated pattern of sounds","c":"有節奏的","s":"The rhythmic sound of the drums filled the street, and soon people began to dance in front of the temple.","t":"有節奏的鼓聲充滿了街道,很快人們就開始在廟前跳起舞來。"},{"w":"sentimental","p":"adj.","d":"connected with feelings and memories, not value","c":"有情感價值的;多愁善感的","s":"The old guitar has sentimental value for my father, because his best friend gave it to him before moving abroad.","t":"這把舊吉他對我爸爸有情感上的價值,因為那是他最好的朋友出國前送他的。"},{"w":"skilful","p":"adj.","d":"very good at doing something","c":"熟練的;技巧高超的","s":"The skilful potter made ten cups in an hour, and every one of them was the same size and shape.","t":"這位技巧高超的陶藝家一小時做了十個杯子,而且每一個的大小和形狀都一樣。"},{"w":"stunning","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or impressive","c":"極美的;令人驚豔的","s":"The photos of the sunrise were stunning, so the magazine used one of them for its front cover.","t":"那些日出照片令人驚豔,所以雜誌用了其中一張當封面。"},{"w":"subdued","p":"adj.","d":"soft and not bright","c":"柔和的;低調的","s":"The café uses subdued lighting in the evening, so customers feel relaxed and stay longer.","t":"這家咖啡廳晚上使用柔和的燈光,所以顧客感到放鬆並待得更久。"},{"w":"superb","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good","c":"極好的;一流的","s":"The actors were superb in the new play, but the story was too long and some people fell asleep.","t":"演員們在新戲中的表現一流,但故事太長,有些人睡著了。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (thought-provoking – unrecognised)","cards":[{"w":"thought-provoking","p":"adj.","d":"making people think seriously","c":"發人深省的","s":"The documentary was thought-provoking, and after watching it our class discussed plastic waste for the whole lesson.","t":"這部紀錄片發人深省,看完後我們班整堂課都在討論塑膠垃圾。"},{"w":"understated","p":"adj.","d":"simple and not trying to attract attention","c":"低調的;含蓄的","s":"Her clothes are always understated, but people notice her because her colours are chosen so carefully.","t":"她的衣著總是很低調,但人們會注意到她,因為她的配色選得非常用心。"},{"w":"unorthodox","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is usual or accepted","c":"非正統的;另類的","s":"The teacher uses unorthodox methods, such as painting with toothbrushes, but her students win many prizes.","t":"這位老師使用另類的方法,例如用牙刷畫畫,但她的學生贏得許多獎項。"},{"w":"aspiring","p":"adj.","d":"hoping to become successful in a job","c":"有抱負的;想成為…的","s":"The workshop is free for aspiring writers, so many university students joined it during the summer holiday.","t":"這個工作坊免費開放給有志成為作家的人,所以許多大學生在暑假參加。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"causing admiration","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"His drawing skills are impressive for a twelve-year-old, so the art teacher entered his work in a national competition.","t":"以十二歲來說,他的繪畫技巧令人印象深刻,所以美術老師把他的作品送去參加全國比賽。"},{"w":"intimate","p":"adj.","d":"small and private, making people feel close","c":"親密的;溫馨的","s":"The singer chose an intimate café for her concert, because she wanted to talk with fans between songs.","t":"這位歌手選了一家溫馨的小咖啡館開演唱會,因為她想在歌曲之間和歌迷聊天。"},{"w":"lyrical","p":"adj.","d":"expressing feelings in a beautiful, song-like way","c":"抒情的","s":"The writer's lyrical descriptions of the countryside are beautiful, so many readers now want to visit the small village.","t":"作者對鄉村抒情的描寫很優美,所以現在許多讀者都想去造訪那座小村莊。"},{"w":"melodramatic","p":"adj.","d":"showing emotions in a very exaggerated way","c":"誇張煽情的","s":"The TV drama is very melodramatic, and the characters cry or shout in almost every scene.","t":"這部電視劇非常誇張煽情,角色幾乎每場戲都在哭或大吼。"},{"w":"monochrome","p":"adj.","d":"using only one colour or black and white","c":"單色的;黑白的","s":"The artist painted the whole room in monochrome grey, so the single red chair in the middle stood out.","t":"藝術家把整個房間漆成單色的灰色,所以中間那把紅椅子格外醒目。"},{"w":"naturalistic","p":"adj.","d":"showing things as they appear in nature","c":"自然主義的;逼真的","s":"The bird paintings are so naturalistic that scientists use them to identify species in the forest.","t":"這些鳥類畫作非常逼真,科學家甚至用它們來辨認森林裡的物種。"},{"w":"neglected","p":"adj.","d":"not given enough attention or care","c":"被忽視的","s":"Many women painters were neglected for centuries, but museums are now bringing their works out of storage.","t":"許多女性畫家數百年來被忽視,但博物館現在正把她們的作品從倉庫中拿出來展示。"},{"w":"obsessive","p":"adj.","d":"thinking about something too much","c":"執著的;過分投入的","s":"He is obsessive about details, so he spent three days painting a single leaf until he was happy.","t":"他對細節非常執著,所以他花了三天畫一片葉子直到滿意為止。"},{"w":"offbeat","p":"adj.","d":"unusual and not what most people expect","c":"另類的;不落俗套的","s":"The band has an offbeat style, and they often play songs with kitchen pots instead of drums.","t":"這個樂團有不落俗套的風格,他們常用廚房的鍋子代替鼓來演奏。"},{"w":"quirky","p":"adj.","d":"unusual in an interesting way","c":"古靈精怪的;奇特的","s":"The café is full of quirky furniture, such as a bathtub sofa, so it is very popular on Instagram.","t":"這家咖啡廳充滿奇特的家具,例如浴缸沙發,所以在Instagram上非常受歡迎。"},{"w":"raw","p":"adj.","d":"natural and not polished","c":"原始的;未經修飾的","s":"The singer's voice sounds raw and honest, so listeners feel that she really means every word.","t":"這位歌手的聲音聽起來未經修飾而真誠,所以聽眾覺得她是真心唱出每一個字。"},{"w":"rebellious","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to follow rules","c":"叛逆的","s":"The rebellious young painters left the art academy, and they held their own exhibition in an old warehouse.","t":"這群叛逆的年輕畫家離開了藝術學院,在一間舊倉庫舉辦了自己的展覽。"},{"w":"reflective","p":"adj.","d":"thinking quietly and deeply","c":"沉思的;深思的","s":"The slow music put me in a reflective mood, so I sat by the window and thought about the past year.","t":"緩慢的音樂讓我進入沉思的心情,所以我坐在窗邊回想過去這一年。"},{"w":"self-indulgent","p":"adj.","d":"doing what pleases yourself without thinking of others","c":"自我陶醉的;放縱自我的","s":"Some critics called the film self-indulgent, because the director made it four hours long and included scenes from his own childhood.","t":"有些評論家說這部電影自我陶醉,因為導演把它拍成四小時,還加入了他自己童年的場景。"},{"w":"sombre","p":"adj.","d":"dark and serious","c":"陰沉的;肅穆的","s":"The war museum uses sombre colours in every room, so visitors naturally speak more quietly inside.","t":"戰爭博物館每個展間都使用肅穆的色調,所以參觀者在裡面自然而然地放低音量。"},{"w":"spiritual","p":"adj.","d":"relating to deep feelings and beliefs rather than the body","c":"心靈的;精神的","s":"For many people, temple music has a spiritual meaning, and it helps them feel calm and connected to their ancestors.","t":"對許多人來說,廟宇音樂具有心靈上的意義,它幫助他們感到平靜並與祖先相連。"},{"w":"stylised","p":"adj.","d":"drawn in a simple, artistic way rather than realistically","c":"風格化的","s":"The cartoon uses stylised characters with huge eyes, but children still find them easy to understand.","t":"這部卡通使用有著大眼睛的風格化角色,但孩子們仍覺得很容易理解。"},{"w":"tasteless","p":"adj.","d":"ugly or offensive, showing bad judgement","c":"品味差的;低俗的","s":"Many people thought the advertisement was tasteless, because it made jokes about a recent disaster.","t":"許多人認為這則廣告低俗,因為它拿最近的災難開玩笑。"},{"w":"tormented","p":"adj.","d":"suffering great mental pain","c":"飽受折磨的","s":"The tormented artist painted dark pictures after losing his son, and his friends worried about his health.","t":"這位飽受折磨的藝術家在失去兒子後畫起了陰暗的作品,朋友們都擔心他的健康。"},{"w":"unfinished","p":"adj.","d":"not completed","c":"未完成的","s":"The composer died before the end of the piece, so the unfinished symphony stops suddenly in the middle of a melody.","t":"作曲家在作品完成前過世,所以這首未完成的交響曲在旋律中途戛然而止。"},{"w":"unrecognised","p":"adj.","d":"not given the respect it deserves","c":"未被賞識的","s":"Her talent remained unrecognised for many years, but a short video online finally made her famous.","t":"她的才華多年來未被賞識,但網路上一段短片終於讓她出名。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (brilliantly – masterfully)","cards":[{"w":"brilliantly","p":"adv.","d":"extremely well or brightly","c":"出色地","s":"The students performed the play brilliantly, and the principal invited them to perform it again for the parents.","t":"學生們出色地演出這齣戲,校長邀請他們再為家長演一次。"},{"w":"critically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that judges carefully","c":"批判性地","s":"We learned to look critically at advertisements, because many of them use beautiful images to hide the truth.","t":"我們學會批判性地看待廣告,因為許多廣告用漂亮的圖像掩蓋真相。"},{"w":"delicately","p":"adv.","d":"in a gentle and careful way","c":"細緻地;輕柔地","s":"The flowers on the vase are delicately painted, and each petal has several shades of pink.","t":"花瓶上的花朵畫得很細緻,每片花瓣都有好幾層粉紅色。"},{"w":"distinctly","p":"adv.","d":"clearly and noticeably","c":"明顯地;清楚地","s":"I distinctly remember my first visit to the art museum, because a guard shouted at me for touching a statue.","t":"我清楚地記得第一次去美術館的情形,因為警衛因我摸了雕像而對我大吼。"},{"w":"effortlessly","p":"adv.","d":"without seeming to try hard","c":"毫不費力地","s":"The dancer moved effortlessly across the stage, but she later said that the routine took her two years to learn.","t":"舞者毫不費力地在舞台上移動,但她後來說這套舞花了她兩年才學會。"},{"w":"exceptionally","p":"adv.","d":"unusually; to a very great degree","c":"格外地;非常","s":"The young cellist is exceptionally talented, so she was invited to study in Vienna when she was only fourteen.","t":"這位年輕大提琴家格外有才華,所以她十四歲就受邀到維也納深造。"},{"w":"faithfully","p":"adv.","d":"exactly and accurately","c":"忠實地","s":"The film faithfully follows the novel, so readers who loved the book will not be disappointed.","t":"這部電影忠實地依循原著小說,所以喜愛這本書的讀者不會失望。"},{"w":"freely","p":"adv.","d":"without being limited or controlled","c":"自由地","s":"In the art room, the children can paint freely, and the teacher never tells them which colours to use.","t":"在美術教室裡,孩子們可以自由地畫畫,老師從不告訴他們該用什麼顏色。"},{"w":"intensely","p":"adv.","d":"very strongly","c":"強烈地;極度地","s":"The actress prepared intensely for the role, and she lived alone in a forest for a month before filming began.","t":"這位女演員為角色極度投入地準備,開拍前她獨自在森林裡住了一個月。"},{"w":"intricately","p":"adv.","d":"with many small, detailed parts","c":"錯綜精細地","s":"The wooden screen is intricately carved with birds and flowers, and it took the craftsman three years to finish.","t":"這座木屏風精細地雕刻著花鳥,工匠花了三年才完成。"},{"w":"intuitively","p":"adv.","d":"by feeling rather than careful thinking","c":"直覺地","s":"The painter chooses colours intuitively, so she never plans the picture before she starts working.","t":"這位畫家憑直覺選擇顏色,所以她開始作畫前從不先規劃畫面。"},{"w":"profoundly","p":"adv.","d":"very deeply","c":"深刻地","s":"The visit to the war memorial profoundly affected the students, and many of them wrote poems about peace afterwards.","t":"參觀戰爭紀念館深刻地影響了學生,之後許多人寫了關於和平的詩。"},{"w":"purely","p":"adv.","d":"only; completely","c":"純粹地","s":"She paints purely for pleasure, so she never sells her work although many people want to buy it.","t":"她純粹為了樂趣而畫畫,所以雖然很多人想買,她從不出售作品。"},{"w":"strikingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very noticeable way","c":"驚人地;顯著地","s":"The two paintings look strikingly similar, so experts believe the same artist painted both of them.","t":"這兩幅畫看起來驚人地相似,所以專家相信它們出自同一位畫家之手。"},{"w":"subtly","p":"adv.","d":"in a slight way that is not easy to notice","c":"微妙地;不著痕跡地","s":"The colours change subtly from blue to green, so you only notice it when you look at the whole painting.","t":"顏色從藍色微妙地轉為綠色,所以只有看整幅畫時才會注意到。"},{"w":"vividly","p":"adv.","d":"very clearly and brightly","c":"生動地;鮮明地","s":"The writer describes the night market so vividly that readers can almost smell the stinky tofu.","t":"作者把夜市描寫得如此生動,讀者幾乎能聞到臭豆腐的味道。"},{"w":"visually","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to seeing","c":"視覺上","s":"The new museum is visually beautiful, but some visitors say the signs are too small to read.","t":"新博物館視覺上很美,但有些參觀者說標示太小看不清楚。"},{"w":"aesthetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to beauty","c":"美學上;外觀上","s":"The new bridge is aesthetically pleasing, and it also allows cyclists to cross the river safely.","t":"這座新橋在美學上令人賞心悅目,也讓自行車騎士能安全過河。"},{"w":"imaginatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a creative way","c":"富想像力地","s":"The old warehouse was imaginatively turned into a library, and children can now read inside giant wooden boats.","t":"這間舊倉庫被富有想像力地改造成圖書館,孩子們現在可以在巨大的木船裡閱讀。"},{"w":"spontaneously","p":"adv.","d":"suddenly and without planning","c":"自發地;即興地","s":"The crowd spontaneously began to sing along with the busker, and soon the whole station was full of music.","t":"群眾自發地跟著街頭藝人唱起歌來,很快整個車站都充滿了音樂。"},{"w":"candidly","p":"adv.","d":"honestly and openly","c":"坦率地","s":"The actor spoke candidly about his failures in the interview, so many young fans felt encouraged by his story.","t":"這位演員在訪談中坦率地談論自己的失敗,所以許多年輕粉絲受到他的故事鼓舞。"},{"w":"consciously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is planned and deliberate","c":"有意識地;刻意地","s":"The designer consciously chose recycled materials, because she wanted her shop to cause less pollution.","t":"這位設計師刻意地選擇回收材料,因為她希望她的店能減少污染。"},{"w":"endlessly","p":"adv.","d":"without stopping","c":"無止盡地;不斷地","s":"The little boy watched the video endlessly, so he could soon copy every dance move perfectly.","t":"這個小男孩不斷地看那支影片,所以他很快就能完美模仿每個舞步。"},{"w":"notoriously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is famous for something bad","c":"出了名地","s":"Art school is notoriously expensive in many countries, so many talented students cannot afford to attend it.","t":"在許多國家,藝術學校出了名地昂貴,所以許多有才華的學生負擔不起。"},{"w":"masterfully","p":"adv.","d":"with great skill","c":"高明地;熟練地","s":"The director masterfully builds tension in the film, and the audience holds its breath during the final scene.","t":"導演在電影中高明地營造緊張感,觀眾在最後一幕都屏住了呼吸。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"art for art's sake","p":"n.phr.","d":"art made only for beauty, not for any other purpose","c":"為藝術而藝術","s":"He does not paint to make money or teach lessons, because he believes in art for art's sake.","t":"他畫畫不是為了賺錢或說教,因為他信奉為藝術而藝術。"},{"w":"a picture is worth a thousand words","p":"n.phr.","d":"an image can explain more than a long description","c":"一圖勝千言","s":"Our teacher showed us one photo of the flood instead of reading the report, because a picture is worth a thousand words.","t":"老師給我們看一張水災的照片而不是念報告,因為一圖勝千言。"},{"w":"beauty is in the eye of the beholder","p":"n.phr.","d":"different people have different ideas of what is beautiful","c":"情人眼裡出西施;美因人而異","s":"My brother thinks the strange sculpture is ugly, but I love it, so I guess beauty is in the eye of the beholder.","t":"我哥覺得那座怪雕塑很醜,但我很喜歡,所以我想美是因人而異的。"},{"w":"the bigger picture","p":"n.phr.","d":"the whole situation, not just small details","c":"大局;全貌","s":"Do not worry too much about one small mistake in your drawing, and try to look at the bigger picture.","t":"不要太擔心畫中的一個小錯誤,試著看看整體大局。"},{"w":"paint a picture of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to describe something in a particular way","c":"描繪出…的樣貌","s":"The documentary paint a picture of life in a poor fishing village, and many viewers decided to donate money.","t":"這部紀錄片描繪出一個貧窮漁村的生活樣貌,許多觀眾因此決定捐款。"},{"w":"draw inspiration from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get ideas for your work from something","c":"從…汲取靈感","s":"Many fashion designers draw inspiration from old movies, so you can see styles from the 1950s in their new collections.","t":"許多時裝設計師從老電影汲取靈感,所以你能在他們的新系列中看到1950年代的風格。"},{"w":"a work of art","p":"n.phr.","d":"a painting, sculpture or other piece of art; something very beautiful","c":"藝術品","s":"The birthday cake was a work of art, and nobody wanted to cut it because it looked like a small castle.","t":"那個生日蛋糕簡直是一件藝術品,沒有人捨得切,因為它看起來像一座小城堡。"},{"w":"a labour of love","p":"n.phr.","d":"hard work done because you love it, not for money","c":"出於熱愛而做的辛苦工作","s":"Restoring the old temple paintings was a labour of love for the artist, because she received almost no money for her years of work.","t":"修復這些古廟畫作對這位藝術家來說是一項出於熱愛的辛苦工作,因為她多年的付出幾乎沒有報酬。"},{"w":"get the creative juices flowing","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help yourself start having ideas","c":"激發創意","s":"I always listen to music before I write, because it helps me get the creative juices flowing.","t":"我寫作前總是聽音樂,因為它幫助我激發創意。"},{"w":"push the boundaries","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to do more than what is usual or accepted","c":"突破界限","s":"The young dancers want to push the boundaries of traditional dance, so they mix Taiwanese folk steps with hip-hop.","t":"這群年輕舞者想要突破傳統舞蹈的界限,所以他們把台灣民俗舞步和嘻哈混搭。"},{"w":"express oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show your feelings and ideas","c":"表達自己","s":"Shy students often find it easier to express oneself through drawing, because they do not need to speak in front of others.","t":"害羞的學生常覺得透過畫畫表達自己比較容易,因為他們不需要在別人面前說話。"},{"w":"steal the show","p":"v.phr.","d":"to attract the most attention in a performance","c":"搶盡風頭","s":"The little girl only had one line in the play, but she steal the show when she started to dance.","t":"那個小女孩在劇中只有一句台詞,但她開始跳舞時就搶盡了風頭。"},{"w":"take centre stage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become the most important or noticed thing","c":"成為焦點","s":"Local artists will take centre stage at this year's festival, while international stars will perform only on the last night.","t":"在今年的藝術節中,在地藝術家將成為焦點,而國際明星只會在最後一晚演出。"},{"w":"a hard act to follow","p":"n.phr.","d":"someone so good that the next person will seem worse","c":"難以超越的榜樣","s":"The last art teacher was very popular, so she will be a hard act to follow for the new teacher.","t":"上一位美術老師非常受歡迎,所以對新老師來說,她會是難以超越的榜樣。"},{"w":"bring something to life","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make something seem real and exciting","c":"使…栩栩如生","s":"The talented actors brought the old story to life, and even students who hated history enjoyed the play.","t":"才華洋溢的演員們讓那個老故事栩栩如生,就連討厭歷史的學生都很喜歡這齣戲。"},{"w":"not one's cup of tea","p":"adj.phr.","d":"not something a person likes","c":"不是某人的菜","s":"Opera is not one's cup of tea, but I still went with my grandmother because she really wanted company.","t":"歌劇不是我的菜,但我還是陪奶奶去了,因為她真的很想要人作伴。"},{"w":"strike a chord","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people feel sympathy or connection","c":"引起共鳴","s":"The song about leaving home strike a chord with many young workers, because they also live far from their families.","t":"那首關於離鄉的歌引起許多年輕上班族的共鳴,因為他們也住得離家人很遠。"},{"w":"behind the scenes","p":"phr.","d":"secretly or in a way the public does not see","c":"在幕後","s":"Many people work behind the scenes at a concert, and without them the singers could not perform.","t":"許多人在演唱會幕後工作,沒有他們,歌手就無法演出。"},{"w":"one of a kind","p":"adj.phr.","d":"completely unique","c":"獨一無二的","s":"Each handmade lamp is one of a kind, so you will never see the same one in another person's house.","t":"每盞手工燈都是獨一無二的,所以你絕不會在別人家看到一模一樣的。"},{"w":"make one's mark","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become successful and noticed","c":"嶄露頭角;留下印記","s":"The young director quickly make one's mark in the film industry, and her first movie won three awards.","t":"這位年輕導演很快就在電影界嶄露頭角,她的第一部電影就贏得了三個獎項。"}]}];
